{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjTTYqBRX3GZXN2rmXRZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01G8ZKhCwdYxtju7wyrBartQ","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-012138__x6981e3/work/PLAN.md","offset":400,"limit":500},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":18648,"cache_read_input_tokens":20226,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":18648},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d022da92-c114-4f47-a8f5-ca68c59e3f52","uuid":"164226b0-d015-45de-881d-3bb54e505bfb","timestamp":"2026-11-05T08:21:49.956Z","request_id":"req_011CgjTTYXpcXdHje2iEA4pD","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01G8ZKhCwdYxtju7wyrBartQ":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-012138__x6981e3/work/PLAN.md","offset":400,"limit":500}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G8ZKhCwdYxtju7wyrBartQ","type":"tool_result","content":"400\t- \"Good morning. You look rested. I can't see. But you felt rested.\"\n401\t- \"Kevin has been with us eleven years. He has never once held a pose.\"\n402\t- \"This is a recording. The person in it is doing better than you.\" *(attract mode)*\n403\t- \"I have been adding seven. To everyone. For years. It felt motivating.\"\n404\t- \"See you tomorrow. Bring your knees.\"\n405\t\n406\t*Coach Plumb:*\n407\t- \"You are a tree. A tree does not check its phone.\"\n408\t- \"Your left knee has wandered off. Please collect it.\"\n409\t- \"Breathe in. Not like that.\"\n410\t- \"Good. Again. That was also good. Again.\"\n411\t- \"Hold. You may blink on Thursday.\"\n412\t- \"I am eighty-one. I say this so that you feel something.\"\n413\t- \"Stillness is a muscle. So is regret. We train both here.\"\n414\t- \"The floor is your friend. It has never once let go.\"\n415\t\n416\t*Classmates:*\n417\t- Marguerite: \"Both hips, new. Knee, new. Opinions, original.\"\n418\t- Dennis: \"I used to do this professionally. Not this. Something near it.\"\n419\t- Dennis: \"It's fine. It's just the one leg.\"\n420\t- June: \"I'm pacing myself.\"\n421\t- June: \"My gran says you're doing your best. She said it very slowly.\"\n422\t\n423\t**Morning questions** (three answers; they change only the remark, and Ounce files them):\n424\t- When you stand up, what sound do you make? *Oof. / Hnng. / I have become the sound.*\n425\t- Have you ever apologised to a chair? *Yes. / Not yet. / It started it.*\n426\t- How many stairs is too many? *One. / All of them. / Depends who's watching.*\n427\t- How do you feel about your ankles? *Fine. / We don't speak. / Which ones?*\n428\t- What is your relationship with the floor? *Distant. / Improving. / It's complicated.*\n429\t- If your knees could talk, what would they say? *Please. / Why. / Nothing. They've given up.*\n430\t- Day 7: Are you happy? *Yes. / No. / Is this graded?* → \"It's all graded.\"\n431\t\n432\t---\n433\t\n434\t## 9. UI and UX: 10 feet, controller first\n435\t\n436\t**One UI for every device: the pixel HUD.** No DOM menus; same screens for pad, keyboard and mouse. Build a small kit in `src/ui/`.\n437\t\n438\t### Layout rules\n439\t\n440\t- **Use `aspect: 'fill'` ✔.** It removes letterboxing at every window size (`adaptive` gives thick black borders at 1280×720). Art size then varies: 480×270 at 1080p and 4K, 427×240 at 720p, 640×360 in a small frame, 400×300 at 800×600. **Lay out from `hud.width` and `hud.height` with anchors**, never fixed coordinates. Keep a 12 art px safe margin.\n441\t- **Pointer to art pixels ✔:** `ax = (p.x + 1) / 2 * hud.width; ay = (1 - p.y) / 2 * hud.height`. The HUD canvas ignores pointer events, and its rect equals the game canvas's.\n442\t- **Text:** the 5×7 font at scale 1 is 20×28 px at 1080p, the minimum. Scale 2 for menu rows and headings, 3-4 for the title and big numbers.\n443\t- **No dense screens:** at most 8 menu rows; at most 3 lines of dialogue; one idea per screen; one activity per records page. Page rather than scroll, wherever you can.\n444\t\n445\t### Mixed-case text ✔\n446\t\n447\tThe engine font is capitals only, which is wrong for this voice. Draw lowercase through `hud.sprite`, everything else through `hud.text`, on a 6 px grid. This table and function rendered correctly; use them:\n448\t\n449\t```js\n450\t// src/ui/font.js. Rows top to bottom, 5 bits, bit 4 = left. Rows 7-8 are descenders.\n451\tconst H = {\n452\ta:'00 00 0e 01 0f 11 0f 00 00', b:'10 10 1e 11 11 11 1e 00 00', c:'00 00 0e 11 10 11 0e 00 00', d:'01 01 0f 11 11 11 0f 00 00',\n453\te:'00 00 0e 11 1f 10 0e 00 00', f:'06 09 08 1c 08 08 08 00 00', g:'00 00 0f 11 11 11 0f 01 0e', h:'10 10 1e 11 11 11 11 00 00',\n454\ti:'04 00 0c 04 04 04 0e 00 00', j:'02 00 06 02 02 02 02 12 0c', k:'10 10 12 14 18 14 12 00 00', l:'0c 04 04 04 04 04 0e 00 00',\n455\tm:'00 00 1a 15 15 15 15 00 00', n:'00 00 1e 11 11 11 11 00 00', o:'00 00 0e 11 11 11 0e 00 00', p:'00 00 1e 11 11 11 1e 10 10',\n456\tq:'00 00 0f 11 11 11 0f 01 01', r:'00 00 16 19 10 10 10 00 00', s:'00 00 0f 10 0e 01 1e 00 00', t:'08 08 1c 08 08 09 06 00 00',\n457\tu:'00 00 11 11 11 13 0d 00 00', v:'00 00 11 11 11 0a 04 00 00', w:'00 00 11 11 15 15 0a 00 00', x:'00 00 11 0a 04 0a 11 00 00',\n458\ty:'00 00 11 11 11 11 0f 01 0e', z:'00 00 1f 02 04 08 1f 00 00' };\n459\texport const GLYPHS = Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(H).map(([k, v]) => [k, v.split(' ').map((h) => parseInt(h, 16).toString(2).padStart(5, '0').replace(/0/g, '.').replace(/1/g, 'o'))]));\n460\texport function say(hud, x, y, text, { color = 'white', shadow = 'ink', scale = 1 } = {}) {\n461\t  for (const ch of text) {\n462\t    const g = GLYPHS[ch];\n463\t    if (g) hud.sprite(x, y, g, { o: color }, { scale, shadow });\n464\t    else if (ch !== ' ') hud.text(x, y, ch, { color, shadow, scale });\n465\t    x += 6 * scale;\n466\t  }\n467\t  return x;\n468\t}\n469\t```\n470\t\n471\tAdd a measuring and word-wrapping helper. Replace any character the font lacks with `?` (hub names can hold anything); a test checks all game text has glyphs.\n472\t\n473\t### Input map\n474\t\n475\tRemap once at boot ✔: `ctx.input.gamepadButtons = { 0:'PadCross', 1:'PadCircle', 2:'PadSquare', 3:'PadTriangle', 4:'PadL1', 5:'PadR1', 6:'PadL2', 7:'PadR2', 8:'PadCreate', 9:'PadOptions', 10:'PadL3', 11:'PadR3', 12:'PadUp', 13:'PadDown', 14:'PadLeft', 15:'PadRight' }`. Pad buttons then appear in `isDown`, `wasPressed`, `state().held` and recordings. Keep one action table in `src/core/actions.js`.\n476\t\n477\t| Action | DualSense (Xbox glyph) | Keyboard | Mouse |\n478\t|---|---|---|---|\n479\t| Lean | Left stick | WASD / arrows; Shift = half | Pointer offset from dial |\n480\t| Confirm | ✕ (A) | Enter, Space, E | Left click on the item |\n481\t| Back | ○ (B) | Esc, Backspace | Right click |\n482\t| Pause | Options (Menu) | Esc, P | Pause icon, top right, shown while the mouse moves |\n483\t| Breath, hold | R2 (RT) or ✕ (A) | Space | Hold left button |\n484\t| Left / right foot | L1 or L2 / R1 or R2 (LB or LT / RB or RT) | F or ← / J or → | Left / right button |\n485\t| Tabs | L1 / R1 (LB / RB) | Q / E | Wheel, or click the tab |\n486\t| Hub: jump, wave, sit | ✕, △, □ (A, Y, X) | Space, V, B | Click to walk |\n487\t\n488\t- **Hero wrapper ✔:** call `readMoveInput(ctx, hero, input)`, then OR in `PadCross` (`consumePress` → `input.jump`, `isDown` → `input.jumpHeld`) and the same for wave and sit. In the hub ✕ interacts when a prompt is showing, otherwise jumps.\n489\t- **Menus** read the d-pad, stick (with repeat), arrows and WASD. Hover moves focus; left click confirms; a wheel scrolls lists; sliders drag.\n490\t- **Keep the mouse native:** the Dot follows the mouse as soon as the mouse moves, and goes back to stick or keys as soon as those are used.\n491\t- **Respect the hub's chord:** ignore Options while Create is held.\n492\t\n493\t### Prompts and glyphs\n494\t\n495\t- Prompts always read `[glyph] verb` and follow the **last device used**. Track it in `src/core/device.js` from `ctx.input`: `held`/`queuedPresses` starting `Pad` or a stick past .3 means pad; `Mouse*` or pointer movement means mouse; anything else means keyboard. Add guarded DOM `keydown`/`pointerdown`/`wheel` listeners for \"press any button\" and for exiting attract.\n496\t- **Glyph sprites, drawn by you in `src/art/glyphs.js`:** PlayStation shapes ✕ ○ □ △ in their colours, L1 R1 L2 R2, Options, sticks. Xbox A B X Y (a Settings option), LB RB LT RT, Menu. Keycaps with the letter. A mouse with the used button lit.\n497\t\n498\t### Screens\n499\t\n500\t- **Dialogue box:** bottom strip, white; speaker name in teal; typewriter at about 40 cps, in sync with voice syllables; ✕ completes, then advances; hold to skip fast. Ounce gets a small dial portrait with a mood needle.\n501\t- **Results, station menu, Hall of Numbers, Locker Room, Sweat Jar, Report:** one focal element each, big numbers, 1-2 lines of comment.\n502\t- **Locker Room:** on a turntable; skin (sand, orange, red, plum), hair style and colour, top, bottom, headband, jar unlocks.\n503\t- **Name entry:** letter grid (stick, d-pad, click) plus direct typing, 8 characters max.\n504\t\n505\t### Pause menu\n506\t\n507\t`engine.timeScale = 0` ✔ freezes physics, `fixedUpdate` and game time while `update` still runs and `wasPressed` still works. Menus therefore read input in `update`. Don't use `engine.paused` for this.\n508\t\n509\tResume / Restart activity / Back to the island / Settings / How to play / About & Credits / **Dev Tools**. In a session: Resume and Settings only, and nothing freezes.\n510\t\n511\t### Settings (own HUD menu, not the engine panel)\n512\t\n513\tMusic volume (**default 10%**), SFX, Voice, Button glyphs (PlayStation / Xbox), Gentle Mode (rings ×1.25, noise ×.8), Mouse lean radius, Step timing offset, Reduce flashes, Look (Default, `storybook`, `arcade`, `handheld`), Pixel size (`engine.settings.set({ look, pixelSize })`), Fullscreen, Reset to defaults.\n514\t\n515\t### Touch-only devices\n516\t\n517\tDetect ✔ `matchMedia('(hover: none) and (pointer: coarse)')` with no gamepad. Start with `touch: false` always, and `settings: { button: 'top-right' }` only on such devices (otherwise `button: false`). ✔ The ⚙ appears and a tap opens the engine's panel. Show over the title: **\"Controller or keyboard required\"**, wrapped: a portrait phone's art is as narrow as 168 px wide. Attract runs and loops. A tap returns to the title message and the 10 s timer restarts. If a pad connects or a key is pressed, drop the message and play normally.\n518\t\n519\t---\n520\t\n521\t## 10. Dev mode\n522\t\n523\tReached from the pause menu, not in sessions. 10-foot legible and fully controller-driven. Tabs with L1/R1.\n524\t\n525\t**Sliders (live, each read by the code every step; registry in `src/core/tunables.js`):**\n526\t\n527\t| Tab | Variables, with defaults |\n528\t|---|---|\n529\t| Balance | dotInstability .6, dotAuthority 3, dotDamping 3.4, dotNoise .8, dotLag .08, ringScale 1, gustForce 1.6, mouseLeanRadius 70 |\n530\t| Breath and reps | breathBonus .55, repLag .10, repFatigue .10, repTempoScale 1 |\n531\t| Rhythm | stepWindow 1, stepOffsetMs 0, hoopLow .9, hoopHigh 2.4, hoopLiftRate .35 |\n532\t| Games | headerInterval 1.0, slackWalkInst 2.6, trayGravity 9.8, trayMaxTilt 14, jogTargetCadence 3, pierBoost 2.14 |\n533\t| Economy | dripRate 1, starThresholdScale 1, ageTrainingWeight .5 |\n534\t\n535\tEach slider shows its value and default. **One button resets the tab, one resets everything.** Export prints the changed values as JSON to the console and copies them if allowed, so a designer can paste them into `src/data/`.\n536\t\n537\t**Tools tab:** go to day 1-7; jump to any activity or scene; finish the current activity with 0-3★; give 50 Drips; unlock all; autopilot (bot skill picker); god mode (Dot can't leave the ring); time scale .25-3; overlay (scene, state, Dot, ring, fps, last device); hide HUD; free camera (`engine.setCamera({ preset: 'free' }, { syncUrl: false })`); dialogue tester (any line, with voice); sound test (every song, SFX, speaker); animation viewer (every clip on an avatar); reset save.\n538\t\n539\t---\n540\t\n541\t## 11. Attract mode\n542\t\n543\tAfter **10 seconds with no input on the title or any menu screen**, start a looping demo:\n544\t\n545\t- **Playlist:** Hub walk → Holding Still → Hoop → Header → Step → Slackline → Tray → Pier Jump → Jog → Long Stand excerpt, about 14 s each, with iris transitions. Cover every activity and feature family.\n546\t- It runs the **real scenes** with expert bot drivers and cheats (ring ×2, god mode). Banner: {TITLE}, \"Press any button.\" plus Ounce's subtitles (\"This is a recording...\").\n547\t- **Any input exits**: key, click, mouse move past a few pixels, wheel, pad button or stick, touch. You return to the title and the timer re-arms.\n548\t- Not in a session, not during play, not on the pause menu.\n549\t\n550\t---\n551\t\n552\t## 12. Multiplayer\n553\t\n554\t**Reading of the brief:** the hub protocol is how the game plays online; on its own the game has no server, so it plays alone or on one screen. Both run the same round, **The Medley**, and the same lane code. Nothing else connects to a network.\n555\t\n556\t### The Medley\n557\t\n558\tThree events in fixed windows: Stillness (a pose), then Beat (Reps or Hoop or Step), then Balance-lean (Header), each 55 s with 10 s between, about 3.2 minutes. The specific picks and shortened durations live in `src/data/medley.js`, and the picks come from a seeded stream. Each event normalises to 0-1000; the total wins. Results show medals, awards (\"Stillest\", \"Most Apologetic\") and Ounce's remarks.\n559\t\n560\t### On its own: Family Hour\n561\t\n562\tJoin screen: **each device claims a mat by pressing Cross/Enter** (up to 4 pads plus keyboard-and-mouse). Bots can fill empty mats (toggle).\n563\t\n564\t**The engine merges all pads into one** ✔, so lanes read `navigator.getGamepads()` by index themselves (`applyDeadzone` is exported; guard for Node). In 4-mat staging, each player gets a small dial (radius 24) above their avatar's head. Podium, rematch.\n565\t\n566\t### In AI Hub: ghost mode\n567\t\n568\tPassed 16/16 with the real engine on WebGPU ✔ at players=1, 2, 4 (latency, jitter, loss) and host-leave.\n569\t\n570\t```html\n571\t<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n572\t<script>/* session.js pasted unmodified: first script, right after charset */</script>\n573\t<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n574\t<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n575\t<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"ghost\">\n576\t<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Score the most across three events. Stay in the circle.\">\n577\t<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Left stick, WASD or mouse: lean. R2, Space or click: breathe. L1/R1, F/J: step.\">\n578\t<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"4\">\n579\t<meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">\n580\t```\n581\t\n582\tBoot order ✔:\n583\t\n584\t```js\n585\tlet info = null;\n586\tif (window.AIHub?.active) info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\n587\tconst engine = await Engine.start(firstScene, withUrlOptions({ /* ... */ seed: info ? info.seed : savedOrDefaultSeed }));\n588\tif (info) AIHub.ready();                 // no key press, as soon as the card can show\n589\t```\n590\t\n591\tIf `connect()` answers null, carry on as the normal game. Without WebGPU, `Engine.start` rejects and the engine prints \"Failed to start: WebGPU unavailable: ...\" on the page ✔. Catch the rejection, or it also surfaces as a page error ✔, and call `AIHub.fail(message)` in a session.\n592\t\n593\t**In a session:**\n594\t- **The card (`card: true`)** is the game's own: the players' avatars lining up on mats in seat colours (`#e8443a #3b82f6 #22c55e #f5b700`), {TITLE}, ready ticks, how to win, the controls for the last device, the time left from the `card` event. Enter or Cross → `AIHub.answer('ready')`; Triangle or M → `AIHub.answer('more')`. Use a **direct `keydown` listener for Enter** ✔ here. No menus. Cosmetic randomness only from `AIHub.rng('card')`.\n595\t- **Start:** on `start` show a countdown from `AIHub.time()`; play at `time() >= 0`. Event windows are read from `AIHub.time()`, so all copies stay in step.\n596\t- **Same world:** gusts, pose picks and object waves come from `AIHub.rng(label)` or the seeded `ctx.random`.\n597\t- **Ghosts:** a `setInterval` at 100 ms (not tied to rendering) sends `AIHub.send({ a: eventIndex, x, y, c: clipIndex, t: clipTime, s: score }, { reliable: false })` and calls `AIHub.progress({ score, label })`. Start as soon as `start` arrives, even with score 0: the harness needs both within seconds. Receivers lerp the other mats; they never simulate them, and they hide a ghost whose `a` differs from theirs.\n598\t- **`leave`:** that avatar waves and walks off. The round goes on, host included.\n599\t- **End:** `AIHub.result({ score, stats, awards })` once, at the end of the Medley or at once on `time-up`. On `end`: stop input, stop sound, send nothing.\n600\t- **Never:** no title, attract, dev mode, saves, quit or restart; no chat or custom names; no `alert`, `window.open` or navigation. Names come from `info.players` and are drawn with `say()`.\n601\t\n602\t---\n603\t\n604\t## 13. Art direction\n605\t\n606\t**Base: the engine's native look**, default pixel pipeline, toon materials, 16-colour palette (`look` left unset). The scene reads clean and bright: white, mist, sky and cyan, with lime and sand for growth and warmth, orange and red as accents. Start with `quality: 'high'` (`'medium'` in sessions, where several copies may share a machine in testing).\n607\t\n608\t**Performance is out of scope.** Add the detail the scene wants and don't spend time on optimisation.\n609\t\n610\t### Avatars ✔\n611\t\n612\tRe-dress the kit's hero with the same rig. This is proven to look good at gameplay framing: egg heads, dot eyes, hair caps. Use `castShadow: false` plus `ContactShadow` ✔: casting on the model gave ugly self-shadow blotches. The hero's `Eyes` mesh reads as sunglasses, so hide it. Compile clips once and share them between avatars.\n613\t\n614\t```js\n615\tfunction soften(mesh, kind = 'prism') { // same bounding box, softer shape\n616\t  mesh.geometry.computeBoundingBox();\n617\t  const b = mesh.geometry.boundingBox, s = b.getSize(new Vector3()), c = b.getCenter(new Vector3());\n618\t  const g = kind === 'egg' ? new SphereGeometry(0.5, 10, 8) : new CylinderGeometry(0.5, 0.5, 1, 8);\n619\t  g.scale(s.x, s.y, s.z); g.translate(c.x, c.y, c.z); mesh.geometry = g;\n620\t}\n621\texport function dress(root, look) { // look: { skin, top, bottom, shoe, hair, long?, bun?, headband? } as palette names\n622\t  const hide = new Set(['Moustache', 'ButtonR', 'ButtonL', 'Hat', 'Brim', 'Eyes', 'Nose']);\n623\t  const SLOT = { Overalls: 'bottom', ThighR: 'bottom', ThighL: 'bottom', ShinR_Mesh: look.long ? 'bottom' : 'skin', ShinL_Mesh: look.long ? 'bottom' : 'skin',\n624\t    Shirt: 'top', SleeveR: 'top', SleeveL: 'top', ForearmR_Mesh: look.long ? 'top' : 'skin', ForearmL_Mesh: look.long ? 'top' : 'skin',\n625\t    GloveR: 'skin', GloveL: 'skin', Face: 'skin', ShoeR: 'shoe', ShoeL: 'shoe' };\n626\t  root.traverse((o) => {\n627\t    if (!o.isMesh) return;\n628\t    if (hide.has(o.name)) { o.visible = false; return; }\n629\t    if (SLOT[o.name]) o.material = toonMaterial(PALETTE[look[SLOT[o.name]]]);\n630\t    if (o.name === 'Face') soften(o, 'egg'); else if (/Sleeve|Forearm|Thigh|Shin|Glove/.test(o.name)) soften(o);\n631\t  });\n632\t  const face = root.getObjectByName('Face'); face.geometry.computeBoundingBox();\n633\t  const fb = face.geometry.boundingBox, size = fb.getSize(new Vector3()), c = fb.getCenter(new Vector3());\n634\t  const add = (m, x, y, z) => { m.position.set(x, y, z); face.parent.add(m); return m; };\n635\t  for (const sx of [-1, 1]) add(new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(0.055, 0.09, 0.03), toonMaterial(PALETTE.ink)), c.x + sx * size.x * 0.2, c.y + 0.02, c.z + size.z * 0.48);\n636\t  add(new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(0.1, 0.022, 0.03), toonMaterial(PALETTE.ink)), c.x, c.y - size.y * 0.2, c.z + size.z * 0.47);\n637\t  const hair = add(new Mesh(new SphereGeometry(0.5, 10, 6, 0, Math.PI * 2, 0, Math.PI * 0.55), toonMaterial(PALETTE[look.hair])), c.x, c.y + size.y * 0.04, c.z - size.z * 0.05);\n638\t  hair.scale.set(size.x * 1.08, size.y * 1.04, size.z * 1.08);\n639\t  if (look.bun) add(new Mesh(new SphereGeometry(0.1, 8, 6), toonMaterial(PALETTE[look.hair])), c.x, c.y + size.y * 0.6, c.z - size.z * 0.2);\n640\t  if (look.headband) { const b2 = add(new Mesh(new CylinderGeometry(0.5, 0.5, 1, 10), toonMaterial(PALETTE[look.headband])), c.x, c.y + size.y * 0.16, c.z); b2.scale.set(size.x * 1.06, 0.06, size.z * 1.06); }\n641\t}\n642\t```\n643\t\n644\tAdd more hair shapes as extra meshes on the head. Good casting: player `{ skin:'sand', top:'white', bottom:'sky', shoe:'white', hair:'ink', headband:'red' }`; Coach `{ skin:'sand', top:'cyan', bottom:'cyan', shoe:'white', hair:'mist', bun:true, long:true }`, plus a plumb bob on a string (`SpringChain`) from her wrist.\n645\t\n646\t### Ounce ✔ (zero problems, zero warnings on the model sheet)\n647\t\n648\t```js\n649\texport const ounce = model({\n650\t  id: 'ounce', about: 'Ounce: a mint retro bathroom scale whose round dial is its face', tags: ['character'], size: [1.1, 1.05, 1.1],\n651\t  palette: { body: 'cyan', base: 'teal', tread: 'sky', face: 'white', rim: 'slate', tick: 'mist', needle: 'red', eye: 'ink' },\n652\t  parts: [\n653\t    { name: 'base', box: [1.04, 0.08, 1.04], at: [0, 0.04, 0], c: 'base' },\n654\t    { name: 'plate', box: [0.96, 0.2, 0.96], at: [0, 0.18, 0], c: 'body' },\n655\t    { mirror: [{ name: 'tread', box: [0.3, 0.03, 0.42], at: [0.22, 0.295, -0.22], c: 'tread' }], axis: 'x' },\n656\t    { group: [\n657\t        { name: 'neck', box: [0.5, 0.42, 0.14], at: [0, 0.21, 0], c: 'body' },\n658\t        { group: [\n659\t            { name: 'rim', cyl: [0.78, 0.1, 0.78], at: [0, 0, 0], c: 'rim', seg: 14 },\n660\t            { name: 'dial', cyl: [0.66, 0.04, 0.66], at: [0, 0.06, 0], c: 'face', seg: 14 },\n661\t            ...[-60, -30, 0, 30, 60].map((a) => ({ box: [0.06, 0.03, 0.09], at: [Math.sin(a * Math.PI / 180) * 0.26, 0.085, -Math.cos(a * Math.PI / 180) * 0.26], rot: [0, -a, 0], c: 'tick' })),\n662\t            { mirror: [{ name: 'eye', box: [0.08, 0.03, 0.11], at: [0.12, 0.09, -0.07], c: 'eye' }], axis: 'x' },\n663\t            { group: [{ name: 'needleBar', box: [0.06, 0.03, 0.22], at: [0, 0, 0.1], c: 'needle' }, { name: 'hub', cyl: [0.07, 0.04, 0.07], at: [0, 0, 0], c: 'needle', seg: 8 }], name: 'needle', pivot: true, at: [0, 0.1, 0.1], rot: [0, 180, 0] },\n664\t          ], name: 'face', pivot: true, at: [0, 0.5, 0.08], rot: [72, 0, 0] },\n665\t      ], name: 'head', pivot: true, at: [0, 0.26, 0.2] },\n666\t  ],\n667\t});\n668\t```\n669\t\n670\tPivots stay movable: `build.object.getObjectByName('needle')` for mood, `'face'` for nods. Scale Ounce ×1.4 on the island and frame close in Weigh-In. Squash on hops.\n671\t\n672\t### Models to write as data (`src/art/models.js`; check each with `node check.mjs --sheets src/art/models.js`)\n673\t\n674\tKettlebell Volcano ✔ (`ball [12,9,12]`, `torus` handle, glowing top), Foam Roller Hill ✔ (a big `cyl` on its side with bands), Dumbbell Bridge ✔, medicine ball ✔, Pavilion ✔ (columns, `cone` roof, recolour per station), Sweat Jar ✔ (`{ lathe: [[.85,0],[.95,.1],[.95,2.1],[.75,2.4],[.75,2.55]], at: [0,.3,0], seg: 12 }` for the glass, plus plinth, lid and label; **toon materials are opaque, so fake the fluid**: a `sky` cylinder 1 cm wider than the wall, scaled in y with Drips, with a white highlight stripe), Rep Shed, Beat Stage with speakers, pier with railings, palm (`tube` trunk, fronds; the library has none), yoga mat, step platform, hoop (`torus`), coconut, flip-flop, golden pineapple, catapult, tray and cups, vitamin, slackline anchors, hammock, lockers, Hall of Numbers board, judges' paddles, mobility scooter, ferry, water cup, sprinkler, Kevin (body, wings, feet, with a two-pose flap).\n675\t\n676\tFrom the library, generic props are fine: `fountain`, `bench`, `lamp-post`, `bush`, `flowers`, `oak`, `fence`, `signpost`, `table`.\n677\t\n678\t### Surfaces and scene effects\n679\t\n680\t- **Tile floor ✔:** `textureDef({ id:'clinic-tile', size:[16,16], tile:true, palette:{ grout:'mist', a:'white', b:'white' }, layers:[{ pattern:'tiles', colors:['grout','a','b'], w:16, h:16, mortar:1, seed:3 }], about:'...', tags:['floor'] })`, added to `TEXTURE_LIBRARY`. **Never stretch a map over a box ✔** (it gave one giant tile): use a `PlaneGeometry` and scale its UVs by metres ÷ (16 / `DEFAULT_TEXEL`), as the kit's market example does.\n681\t- **World:** `WaterSurface` ✔, `GrassField` ✔, sand and lawn as flat boxes ✔, `RippleField` at splashes, `Precipitation` in the finale, `Boids` gulls, `Decals` footprints on sand.\n682\t- **Light:** `ctx.lights` for pavilion lanterns at dusk; `applySky(skyAt(h))` for morning and evening.\n683\t- **Game feel:** `hitstop`, `shake`, `screen.flash`, `screen.shockwave` on the splash, iris transitions (`screen.cover`/`reveal` ✔, also resolve headless), `Trail` behind the jogger, custom particles ('sweat' in cyan, 'confetti', 'splash', 'zen' motes).\n684\t- **Cutscenes:** ferry arrival, confession and ending with `Timeline` ✔. On the `fixed` preset, apply `tl.camera()` each frame to `ctx.camera.camera` (position, `lookAt`, fov, `updateProjectionMatrix`) ✔. Use `tl.line()` for subtitles, `tl.bars()` for letterbox.\n685\t\n686\t---\n687\t\n688\t## 14. Animation\n689\t\n690\tUse the engine's native system: `ClipDef` data, `compileClips`, `THREE.AnimationMixer` for class avatars, `PlatformerCharacter` on the island, procedural layers (`Squash`, `SpringChain`) for character.\n691\t\n692\t**Conventions** (`HERO_RIG`): facing +Z. Arm X: -90 ahead, -180 overhead. Arm Z: out to the side (R negative, L positive). Forearm -X bends the elbow. Leg -X swings forward. Shin +X bends the knee. Foot +X points the toes. Pelvis `p` offsets, `r` tips the whole body. Torso +X bends forward.\n693\t\n694\t**Verified poses ✔** (`validateClip` clean, `analyzeClip` no problems, reviewed on contact sheets):\n695\t\n696\t```js\n697\tconst hold = (name, pose) => ({ name, frames: 60, loop: true, keys: [[0, pose], [60, pose]] });\n698\tconst feet = (pose, R, L) => placeFeet(pose, HERO_RIG, { R, L });\n699\thold('Tree', { Pelvis: { p: [0.03, -0.02, 0] }, ArmR: [-172, 0, -6], ForearmR: [-14, 0, 0], ArmL: [-172, 0, 6], ForearmL: [-14, 0, 0], LegR: [-62, 0, -58], ShinR: [150, 0, 0], FootR: [30, 0, 0] });\n700\thold('Heron', { Pelvis: { p: [0, -0.02, 0] }, Torso: [10, 0, 0], Head: [-14, 0, 0], ArmR: [-20, 0, -80], ArmL: [-20, 0, 80], ForearmR: [-30, 0, 0], ForearmL: [-30, 0, 0], LegR: [-85, 0, 0], ShinR: [95, 0, 0], FootR: [35, 0, 0] });\n701\thold('Warrior', feet({ Pelvis: { p: [0, -0.2, 0] }, Torso: [0, 25, 0], Head: [0, 40, 0], ArmR: [0, 0, -90], ArmL: [0, 0, 90] }, { z: 0.38 }, { z: -0.38 }));\n702\thold('Chair', feet({ Pelvis: { p: [0, -0.28, -0.06] }, Torso: [24, 0, 0], Head: [-18, 0, 0], ArmR: [-110, 0, -8], ArmL: [-110, 0, 8] }, { z: 0 }, { z: 0 }));\n703\thold('Fold', feet({ Pelvis: { p: [0, -0.03, -0.03] }, Torso: [88, 0, 0], Head: [10, 0, 0], ArmR: [-70, 0, -6], ArmL: [-70, 0, 6], ForearmR: [-8, 0, 0], ForearmL: [-8, 0, 0] }, { z: 0 }, { z: 0 }));\n704\thold('Plank', { Pelvis: { r: [66, 0, 0], p: [0, -0.2, 0] }, Head: [-48, 0, 0], ArmR: [-63, 0, -5], ArmL: [-63, 0, 5], HandR: [-40, 0, 0], HandL: [-40, 0, 0], FootR: [55, 0, 0], FootL: [55, 0, 0] });\n705\t// Scrubbed reps: keys built with placeFeet AND a feet track, or the sole dips through the floor mid-clip.\n706\tconst squatTop = { Pelvis: { p: [0, -0.02, 0] }, Torso: [2, 0, 0], ArmR: [6, 0, -9], ArmL: [6, 0, 9] }, squatLow = { Pelvis: { p: [0, -0.3, -0.05] }, Torso: [26, 0, 0], Head: [-20, 0, 0], ArmR: [-85, 0, -8], ArmL: [-85, 0, 8] };\n707\t({ name: 'SquatRep', frames: 30, grounded: true, keys: [[0, feet(squatTop, { z: 0 }, { z: 0 })], [30, feet(squatLow, { z: 0 }, { z: 0 })]], feet: [[0, { R: { z: 0 }, L: { z: 0 } }], [30, { R: { z: 0 }, L: { z: 0 } }]] });\n708\t// LungeRep: the same way, low pose Pelvis p [0,-0.24,0], Torso [6,0,0], goals R { z: .34 }, L { z: -.32, pitch: 25, pivot: 'ball' }. For the left side, map poses through mirror(pose, HERO_RIG) and swap R and L goals.\n709\t```\n710\t\n711\t**Still to author:** Press; StepL/StepR; header nod; flail; daze; bow; slow clap; sneeze; Coach's point and demonstration transitions; tuck and cannonball; judge raising a paddle; stepping onto Ounce; ferry disembark. Reuse kit clips: `Idle`, `Walk`, `Run`, `Sit`, `LieIdle`, `Wave`, `Victory`, `Teeter`, `Hurt`, `Fall`, `GetUp`, and more (`HERO_CLIPS`).\n712\t\n713\t**Preview without a GPU ✔:** `tools/clip-sheet.mjs` uses `renderSheet(model, HERO_RIG, def, clip, { frames, views: ['front', 'side'], scale: 90, trails: false, skeleton: false })` → `{ width, height, data }`, written as a PNG with `node:zlib` (`deflateSync`, `crc32`). Look at every new pose once. Hide the hat and moustache first so you judge the real silhouette.\n714\t\n715\t---\n716\t\n717\t## 15. Audio\n718\t\n719\tEverything is written in code. No audio files.\n720\t\n721\t### Music\n722\t\n723\t- **`ctx.audio.setVolume('music', savedMusic ?? 0.10)` at boot, every boot**, from your own settings key. The engine's default is 60%, and its stored volume key (`pixel-engine:audio`) is shared by every engine game on the origin, so don't rely on it.\n724\t- **Write instruments loud:** track `volume` 0.45-0.8. The kit's examples use about 0.12, written for a 60% bus; at 10% × master .8 that is near silence. A test checks each song: sum of track volumes × 0.1 × 0.8 ≥ 0.03.\n725\t- Songs are `Song` data, in `src/audio/songs.js`, each original, none imitating the source:\n726\t\n727\t| Song | Feel |\n728\t|---|---|\n729\t| Title / Plaza | gentle waiting-room bossa, about 92 BPM, soft triangle plucks |\n730\t| Holding Still | slow, sparse, breath-paced, 60 BPM |\n731\t| Rep Shed | light funk bass, 110 BPM |\n732\t| Beat Beach (Hoop) and Step Class | bright, four-on-the-floor; Step is 104 BPM exactly |\n733\t| Lagoon Games | staccato ukulele feel, 120 BPM |\n734\t| Jog | steady, cheerful, 112 BPM |\n735\t| Evening Report | music box, 70 BPM |\n736\t| Long Stand | near silence, then one swelling chord line at t = 75 |\n737\t\n738\t### SFX\n739\t\n740\t`ctx.audio.register` data: needle tick, ring chime in/out, wobble warning, rep tick, step perfect/good, combo, coconut bonk, flip-flop thwap, hoop whirr (`loop`), splash, gust, gull squawk, jar drip, star pop, menu move/confirm/back, \"Ow\" stinger.\n741\t\n742\t### Voices: Animalese/Simlish gibberish\n743\t\n744\tBuild in `src/audio/voice.js`:\n745\t\n746\t1. **`syllabify(text, speaker)` is pure and testable in Node.** Words split into syllables; a hash of each word picks consonant class and vowel, so **the same word always sounds the same**. Output: `[{ t, dur, f0, vowel, cons, charIndex }]`. Declination -15% across a sentence; `?` rises 25% at the end; `!` +15%; `...` slows. The dialogue typewriter reads `charIndex`.\n747\t2. **`renderVoice(ctx, destination, syllables, when)`** schedules, per syllable: a saw oscillator at `f0` through two parallel bandpass filters at the vowel's formants (a 800/1200, e 500/1900, i 300/2300, o 500/900, u 350/800, × speaker shift), gain envelope 6 ms up, 30 ms down; a noise burst for plosives (8 ms) and fricatives (40 ms).\n748\t3. **Routing:** it works on any `BaseAudioContext`, so it renders in `OfflineAudioContext` for tests. Live, use `ctx.audio.context`, connected to `ctx.audio.buses.sfx` (undocumented but present in 0.46.0, so master and mute apply) via your own Voice gain. `ctx.audio.context` is null headless and before the first input: no-op and log.\n749\t\n750\t| Speaker | f0 | Syllables/s | Formant shift | Extra |\n751\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n752\t| Ounce | 340 | 13 | ×1.25 | a needle tick on punctuation |\n753\t| Coach | 165 | 7.5 | ×.9 | flat pitch, long pauses |\n754\t| Marguerite | 230 | 9 | ×1 | slight vibrato |\n755\t| Dennis | 120 | 11 | ×.95 | pitch up on last word |\n756\t| June | 300 | 10 | ×1.15 | no contour at all |\n757\t| Kevin | | | | squawk SFX, never words |\n758\t\n759\t---\n760\t\n761\t## 16. Architecture\n762\t\n763\tDownload the kit (the URL is in your brief) and copy the contents of the zip's top-level `pixel-engine/` folder into the dev folder, so `pixel-engine.js`, `check.mjs` and the guides sit at its root. **Never edit `pixel-engine.js`**: record its sha256 in `vendor/pixel-engine.sha256` when you unzip, and a test compares it. Fetch the hub's `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` and `README.md` into `vendor/hub/` from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/`.\n764\t\n765\t```\n766\tpixel-engine.js  check.mjs  GUIDE.md ...        the kit, untouched\n767\tvendor/hub/                                     hub client and harness, untouched\n768\tsrc/main.js                                     boot: session check, Engine.start, first scene\n769\tsrc/app.js                                      App: scene switching, save, settings, tunables, device, debug API\n770\tsrc/core/      dot.js drivers.js actions.js device.js tunables.js save.js net.js clock.js\n771\tsrc/ui/        font.js menu.js dialogue.js widgets.js prompts.js screens/*\n772\tsrc/audio/     voice.js songs.js sfx.js\n773\tsrc/art/       avatar.js models.js textures.js clips.js glyphs.js portraits.js\n774\tsrc/data/      title.js activities.js poses.js reps.js charts.js boards.js week.js lines.js\n775\t               questions.js unlocks.js classmates.js stations.js medley.js about.js\n776\tsrc/scenes/    base.js boot.js title.js attract.js hub.js weighin.js report.js locker.js records.js jar.js\n777\t               card.js medley.js join.js ending.js  activity/{base,poses,reps,hoop,step,header,slackline,tray,jog,pier,longstand}.js\n778\ttools/         build.mjs test.mjs clip-sheet.mjs shot.mjs\n779\ttests/         headless/*.mjs  browser/*.mjs\n780\t```\n781\t\n782\t**Everything a designer would change is plain data in `src/data/`:** poses, exercises, charts, boards, schedules, lines, unlocks, stars. A new pose, chart, board or day needs no code. That is what lets the rest of the game be built out later with normal tools, together with the live sliders and their JSON export.\n783\t\n784\t**Engine patterns:**\n785\t- Start ✔: `Engine.start(new Boot(), withUrlOptions({ container: document.getElementById('app'), aspect: 'fill', touch: false, settings: { button: touchOnly ? 'top-right' : false }, quality: info ? 'medium' : 'high', seed, background: PALETTE.sky, camera }))`.\n786\t- Each scene is a `Game`, swapped with `engine.loadGame(scene, { camera })`. It frees everything per level; keep persistent state in `App`. Transition: `await screen.cover('iris')`, `await loadGame`, `await screen.reveal('iris')`.\n787\t- `BaseScene` owns the frame order: `update` → `App.device.update` → overlays (pause, dialogue, dev) take input first → the scene's own update → `hud.clear()` → scene draw → overlays draw. Gameplay goes in `fixedUpdate`, skipped automatically while `timeScale` is 0.\n788\t- **Rules from the guide that matter here:** gameplay in `fixedUpdate` with `consumePress`; `wasPressed` only in `update`; all randomness from `ctx.random` forks (never `Math.random`); time from `ctx.time` (never `performance.now`); no `new PointLight`. Modules guard `document`, `window`, `navigator` and `localStorage`, so **everything runs in Node** ✔.\n789\t- **Drivers** (`src/core/drivers.js`): `read(out)` fills `{ x, y, breath, stepL, stepR, confirm }`. `LocalDriver` (engine input and mouse), `PadDriver(index)` (Family Hour), `BotDriver(skill)`, `GhostDriver` (display only). Attract, tests, classmates and online all reuse this one seam.\n790\t- **Debug API**, kept in the shipped game (`globalThis.__GAME__ = App`): `go(id, args)`, `state()` as JSON, `setDriver(skill)`, `tunables`. Give every scene a real `status()` line (`activity hoop | play | t 31.2 | score 412`) and a `fingerprint()` (score, Dot state).\n791\t\n792\t---\n793\t\n794\t## 17. Verified recipes\n795\t\n796\t### Single-file build ✔ (boots on `file://` in about 1.3 s; passes `check.mjs` and the harness)\n797\t\n798\t```js\n799\t// tools/build.mjs (esbuild is on this machine)\n800\texecFileSync('esbuild', ['src/main.js', '--bundle', '--format=esm', '--platform=browser', '--target=esnext', '--charset=utf8', '--outfile=.build/bundle.js', '--log-level=warning'], { stdio: 'inherit' });\n801\tconst safe = (s) => s.replace(/<\\/script/gi, '<\\\\/script').replace(/<!--/g, '<\\\\!--');\n802\tconst html = `<!doctype html>\n803\t<html lang=\"en\"><head>\n804\t<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n805\t<script>${readFileSync('vendor/hub/session.js', 'utf8')}</script>\n806\t${HUB_METAS}\n807\t<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, maximum-scale=1, user-scalable=no, viewport-fit=cover\">\n808\t<link rel=\"icon\" href=\"data:,\"><title>${TITLE}</title>\n809\t<style>html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: #0d0b14; } #app { position: fixed; inset: 0; }</style>\n810\t</head><body><div id=\"app\"></div>\n811\t<script type=\"module\">${safe(readFileSync('.build/bundle.js', 'utf8'))}</script>\n812\t</body></html>`;\n813\twriteFileSync(OUTPUT_HTML, html);   // OUTPUT_HTML: the deliverable name your brief gives, in root\n814\t```\n815\t\n816\tThe session client goes in **unmodified**: the hub replaces an unmodified copy with each new version. Nothing is fetched at runtime, so the game needs no CDN. Bundling doesn't count as editing the engine; `pixel-engine.js` itself stays byte-identical. Output is about 5.4 MB.\n817\t\n818\t### Browser flags ✔\n819\t\n820\t**Use all five.** With only the three in the machine notes, `renderer.capture()` failed: `mapAsync ... A valid external Instance reference no longer exists`.\n821\t\n822\t```\n823\t--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader\n824\t```\n825\t\n826\t### Node Playwright and the kit's check ✔\n827\t\n828\t`npm install playwright@1.63.0` in the dev folder. Then `node check.mjs <page> --keys KeyD*30` works on the built html if it's copied into the dev folder.\n829\t\n830\t### Screenshots ✔\n831\t\n832\tThe live loop rejects `capture()`, and a WebGPU canvas may screenshot blank. So step first, and composite the HUD:\n833\t\n834\t```js\n835\tconst e = window.__PIXEL_ENGINE__; e.step(30);          // switches to manual time\n836\tconst f = await e.renderer.capture();                   // { width, height, pixels }\n837\tconst c = document.createElement('canvas'); c.width = f.width; c.height = f.height;\n838\tconst g = c.getContext('2d'); g.putImageData(new ImageData(new Uint8ClampedArray(f.pixels), f.width, f.height), 0, 0);\n839\tg.imageSmoothingEnabled = false; if (e.hud.canvas?.width) g.drawImage(e.hud.canvas, 0, 0, f.width, f.height);\n840\treturn c.toDataURL('image/png');\n841\t```\n842\t\n843\tPut this in `tools/shot.mjs <scene> [--size 1920x1080]`. Use it only for what a script can't judge: composition and legibility. Judge the 10-foot view at 1920×1080.\n844\t\n845\t### Gamepad stub ✔\n846\t\n847\tAdd as an init script; change the state from the test:\n848\t\n849\t```js\n850\twindow.__pad = { buttons: Array.from({ length: 17 }, () => ({ pressed: false, value: 0, touched: false })), axes: [0, 0, 0, 0] };\n851\tnavigator.getGamepads = () => [{ id: 'Stub', index: 0, connected: true, mapping: 'standard', timestamp: performance.now(), axes: __pad.axes, buttons: __pad.buttons }, null, null, null];\n852\t```\n853\t\n854\tRead inputs through a frame: `moveAxis()` gave (0.8, 0.6) for axes (0.8, -0.6) in-game. Headless, `e.input.setKey('PadCross', true)` works without any stub ✔.\n855\t\n856\t### Hub harness ✔\n857\t\n858\tCopy the built html (as `game.html`) with `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` into a temp folder inside the dev folder. Serve it with `python3 -u -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` ✔, reading the port from its first output line and stopping it by its PID. An in-process `node:http` server on `127.0.0.1` and port 0 also works, but it must send `Content-Type: text/javascript` for `.js`, or the harness's module imports fail. Then for each of:\n859\t\n860\t```\n861\tharness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=1\n862\tharness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=2\n863\tharness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5\n864\tharness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&scenario=host-leave\n865\t```\n866\t\n867\twait for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`, then require `window.__hubCheck.pass`; print failed checks' `name` and `detail`. Each took 10-13 s with a light scene. Keep the card scene light so `ready()` lands inside the 20 s limit even with 4 software-rendered copies. Confirm the served page is yours (its title) before trusting a result. Then open the game outside a session and check it still runs.\n868\t\n869\t### Headless facts ✔\n870\t\n871\t- 600 frames with mixers takes about 80 ms, and boot about 240 ms, so full playthroughs are cheap.\n872\t- `Engine.headless(game, { camera })`: built-ins load with no asset reader.\n873\t- `recording()` and `replay()` reproduce the fingerprint across `loadGame`.\n874\t- `input.setPointer(x, y, true)` drives the mouse.\n875\t- `ctx.audio` counts plays with no context.\n876\t\n877\t---\n878\t\n879\t## 18. Testing\n880\t\n881\t**One command: `node tools/test.mjs`** prints only failures and one count line (`212/212 passed`). `--fast` runs the Node tests only. Rerun only after changing what a test covers. Prefer scripts to screenshots. Don't use subagents or workflows to review, judge or audit. Keep at most two browsers open.\n882\t\n883\t**Headless (Node), seconds:**\n884\t\n885\t1. **Dot:** idle bot < 20% at ring .30; average 35-65%; good > 80%; expert > 95%.\n886\t2. **Clips:** `validateClip` empty and `analyzeClip(...).problems` empty for every clip you wrote.\n887\t3. **Data:** every model (`checkModel`) and texture (`validateTexture`) clean; all ids resolve; `parseSong` on every song; each song passes the level check in §15; every line fits its box; every character of every string has a glyph.\n888\t4. **Every activity:** idle bot finishes with 0★ and no error; expert bot ≥ 2★ (≥ 3★ on easy ones); sloppy < expert; result written; Drips correct.\n889\t5. **Full scripted playthrough:** drive the real menus with `setKey` from a fresh save, bots inside activities: new week → all 7 days → every station → goals → unlock schedule → Jar milestones → Long Stand → confession subtracts exactly 7 → credits → Week 2. Assert the state at each step.\n890\t6. **Save:** reload mid-week restores; corrupt JSON falls back safely; no storage works.\n891\t7. **Pause:** `timeScale` 0, `fixedUpdate` frozen, menu navigable, resume exact.\n892\t8. **Dev:** every slider changes live behaviour; reset restores defaults; every tool works.\n893\t9. **Attract:** 10 s idle on title and on a menu starts it; no trigger during play; a full loop runs error-free over all items; any input exits.\n894\t10. **Determinism:** record an activity, replay it, fingerprints equal.\n895\t11. **Medley:** 4 bot lanes, scores in range, windows respected; a ghost lane never simulates.\n896\t12. **Voice:** `syllabify` is stable, the same word gives the same syllables, a question rises.\n897\t13. **Engine untouched:** `pixel-engine.js` hash equals the kit's.\n898\t\n899\t**Browser, on the built html via `file://`:**"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d022da92-c114-4f47-a8f5-ca68c59e3f52","uuid":"de5b51b8-5150-4114-a673-a2395a5a1dc5","timestamp":"2026-11-05T08:21:50.100Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-012138__x6981e3/work/PLAN.md","content":"- \"Good morning. You look rested. I can't see. But you felt rested.\"\n- \"Kevin has been with us eleven years. He has never once held a pose.\"\n- \"This is a recording. The person in it is doing better than you.\" *(attract mode)*\n- \"I have been adding seven. To everyone. For years. It felt motivating.\"\n- \"See you tomorrow. Bring your knees.\"\n\n*Coach Plumb:*\n- \"You are a tree. A tree does not check its phone.\"\n- \"Your left knee has wandered off. Please collect it.\"\n- \"Breathe in. Not like that.\"\n- \"Good. Again. That was also good. Again.\"\n- \"Hold. You may blink on Thursday.\"\n- \"I am eighty-one. I say this so that you feel something.\"\n- \"Stillness is a muscle. So is regret. We train both here.\"\n- \"The floor is your friend. It has never once let go.\"\n\n*Classmates:*\n- Marguerite: \"Both hips, new. Knee, new. Opinions, original.\"\n- Dennis: \"I used to do this professionally. Not this. Something near it.\"\n- Dennis: \"It's fine. It's just the one leg.\"\n- June: \"I'm pacing myself.\"\n- June: \"My gran says you're doing your best. She said it very slowly.\"\n\n**Morning questions** (three answers; they change only the remark, and Ounce files them):\n- When you stand up, what sound do you make? *Oof. / Hnng. / I have become the sound.*\n- Have you ever apologised to a chair? *Yes. / Not yet. / It started it.*\n- How many stairs is too many? *One. / All of them. / Depends who's watching.*\n- How do you feel about your ankles? *Fine. / We don't speak. / Which ones?*\n- What is your relationship with the floor? *Distant. / Improving. / It's complicated.*\n- If your knees could talk, what would they say? *Please. / Why. / Nothing. They've given up.*\n- Day 7: Are you happy? *Yes. / No. / Is this graded?* → \"It's all graded.\"\n\n---\n\n## 9. UI and UX: 10 feet, controller first\n\n**One UI for every device: the pixel HUD.** No DOM menus; same screens for pad, keyboard and mouse. Build a small kit in `src/ui/`.\n\n### Layout rules\n\n- **Use `aspect: 'fill'` ✔.** It removes letterboxing at every window size (`adaptive` gives thick black borders at 1280×720). Art size then varies: 480×270 at 1080p and 4K, 427×240 at 720p, 640×360 in a small frame, 400×300 at 800×600. **Lay out from `hud.width` and `hud.height` with anchors**, never fixed coordinates. Keep a 12 art px safe margin.\n- **Pointer to art pixels ✔:** `ax = (p.x + 1) / 2 * hud.width; ay = (1 - p.y) / 2 * hud.height`. The HUD canvas ignores pointer events, and its rect equals the game canvas's.\n- **Text:** the 5×7 font at scale 1 is 20×28 px at 1080p, the minimum. Scale 2 for menu rows and headings, 3-4 for the title and big numbers.\n- **No dense screens:** at most 8 menu rows; at most 3 lines of dialogue; one idea per screen; one activity per records page. Page rather than scroll, wherever you can.\n\n### Mixed-case text ✔\n\nThe engine font is capitals only, which is wrong for this voice. Draw lowercase through `hud.sprite`, everything else through `hud.text`, on a 6 px grid. This table and function rendered correctly; use them:\n\n```js\n// src/ui/font.js. Rows top to bottom, 5 bits, bit 4 = left. Rows 7-8 are descenders.\nconst H = {\na:'00 00 0e 01 0f 11 0f 00 00', b:'10 10 1e 11 11 11 1e 00 00', c:'00 00 0e 11 10 11 0e 00 00', d:'01 01 0f 11 11 11 0f 00 00',\ne:'00 00 0e 11 1f 10 0e 00 00', f:'06 09 08 1c 08 08 08 00 00', g:'00 00 0f 11 11 11 0f 01 0e', h:'10 10 1e 11 11 11 11 00 00',\ni:'04 00 0c 04 04 04 0e 00 00', j:'02 00 06 02 02 02 02 12 0c', k:'10 10 12 14 18 14 12 00 00', l:'0c 04 04 04 04 04 0e 00 00',\nm:'00 00 1a 15 15 15 15 00 00', n:'00 00 1e 11 11 11 11 00 00', o:'00 00 0e 11 11 11 0e 00 00', p:'00 00 1e 11 11 11 1e 10 10',\nq:'00 00 0f 11 11 11 0f 01 01', r:'00 00 16 19 10 10 10 00 00', s:'00 00 0f 10 0e 01 1e 00 00', t:'08 08 1c 08 08 09 06 00 00',\nu:'00 00 11 11 11 13 0d 00 00', v:'00 00 11 11 11 0a 04 00 00', w:'00 00 11 11 15 15 0a 00 00', x:'00 00 11 0a 04 0a 11 00 00',\ny:'00 00 11 11 11 11 0f 01 0e', z:'00 00 1f 02 04 08 1f 00 00' };\nexport const GLYPHS = Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(H).map(([k, v]) => [k, v.split(' ').map((h) => parseInt(h, 16).toString(2).padStart(5, '0').replace(/0/g, '.').replace(/1/g, 'o'))]));\nexport function say(hud, x, y, text, { color = 'white', shadow = 'ink', scale = 1 } = {}) {\n  for (const ch of text) {\n    const g = GLYPHS[ch];\n    if (g) hud.sprite(x, y, g, { o: color }, { scale, shadow });\n    else if (ch !== ' ') hud.text(x, y, ch, { color, shadow, scale });\n    x += 6 * scale;\n  }\n  return x;\n}\n```\n\nAdd a measuring and word-wrapping helper. Replace any character the font lacks with `?` (hub names can hold anything); a test checks all game text has glyphs.\n\n### Input map\n\nRemap once at boot ✔: `ctx.input.gamepadButtons = { 0:'PadCross', 1:'PadCircle', 2:'PadSquare', 3:'PadTriangle', 4:'PadL1', 5:'PadR1', 6:'PadL2', 7:'PadR2', 8:'PadCreate', 9:'PadOptions', 10:'PadL3', 11:'PadR3', 12:'PadUp', 13:'PadDown', 14:'PadLeft', 15:'PadRight' }`. Pad buttons then appear in `isDown`, `wasPressed`, `state().held` and recordings. Keep one action table in `src/core/actions.js`.\n\n| Action | DualSense (Xbox glyph) | Keyboard | Mouse |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Lean | Left stick | WASD / arrows; Shift = half | Pointer offset from dial |\n| Confirm | ✕ (A) | Enter, Space, E | Left click on the item |\n| Back | ○ (B) | Esc, Backspace | Right click |\n| Pause | Options (Menu) | Esc, P | Pause icon, top right, shown while the mouse moves |\n| Breath, hold | R2 (RT) or ✕ (A) | Space | Hold left button |\n| Left / right foot | L1 or L2 / R1 or R2 (LB or LT / RB or RT) | F or ← / J or → | Left / right button |\n| Tabs | L1 / R1 (LB / RB) | Q / E | Wheel, or click the tab |\n| Hub: jump, wave, sit | ✕, △, □ (A, Y, X) | Space, V, B | Click to walk |\n\n- **Hero wrapper ✔:** call `readMoveInput(ctx, hero, input)`, then OR in `PadCross` (`consumePress` → `input.jump`, `isDown` → `input.jumpHeld`) and the same for wave and sit. In the hub ✕ interacts when a prompt is showing, otherwise jumps.\n- **Menus** read the d-pad, stick (with repeat), arrows and WASD. Hover moves focus; left click confirms; a wheel scrolls lists; sliders drag.\n- **Keep the mouse native:** the Dot follows the mouse as soon as the mouse moves, and goes back to stick or keys as soon as those are used.\n- **Respect the hub's chord:** ignore Options while Create is held.\n\n### Prompts and glyphs\n\n- Prompts always read `[glyph] verb` and follow the **last device used**. Track it in `src/core/device.js` from `ctx.input`: `held`/`queuedPresses` starting `Pad` or a stick past .3 means pad; `Mouse*` or pointer movement means mouse; anything else means keyboard. Add guarded DOM `keydown`/`pointerdown`/`wheel` listeners for \"press any button\" and for exiting attract.\n- **Glyph sprites, drawn by you in `src/art/glyphs.js`:** PlayStation shapes ✕ ○ □ △ in their colours, L1 R1 L2 R2, Options, sticks. Xbox A B X Y (a Settings option), LB RB LT RT, Menu. Keycaps with the letter. A mouse with the used button lit.\n\n### Screens\n\n- **Dialogue box:** bottom strip, white; speaker name in teal; typewriter at about 40 cps, in sync with voice syllables; ✕ completes, then advances; hold to skip fast. Ounce gets a small dial portrait with a mood needle.\n- **Results, station menu, Hall of Numbers, Locker Room, Sweat Jar, Report:** one focal element each, big numbers, 1-2 lines of comment.\n- **Locker Room:** on a turntable; skin (sand, orange, red, plum), hair style and colour, top, bottom, headband, jar unlocks.\n- **Name entry:** letter grid (stick, d-pad, click) plus direct typing, 8 characters max.\n\n### Pause menu\n\n`engine.timeScale = 0` ✔ freezes physics, `fixedUpdate` and game time while `update` still runs and `wasPressed` still works. Menus therefore read input in `update`. Don't use `engine.paused` for this.\n\nResume / Restart activity / Back to the island / Settings / How to play / About & Credits / **Dev Tools**. In a session: Resume and Settings only, and nothing freezes.\n\n### Settings (own HUD menu, not the engine panel)\n\nMusic volume (**default 10%**), SFX, Voice, Button glyphs (PlayStation / Xbox), Gentle Mode (rings ×1.25, noise ×.8), Mouse lean radius, Step timing offset, Reduce flashes, Look (Default, `storybook`, `arcade`, `handheld`), Pixel size (`engine.settings.set({ look, pixelSize })`), Fullscreen, Reset to defaults.\n\n### Touch-only devices\n\nDetect ✔ `matchMedia('(hover: none) and (pointer: coarse)')` with no gamepad. Start with `touch: false` always, and `settings: { button: 'top-right' }` only on such devices (otherwise `button: false`). ✔ The ⚙ appears and a tap opens the engine's panel. Show over the title: **\"Controller or keyboard required\"**, wrapped: a portrait phone's art is as narrow as 168 px wide. Attract runs and loops. A tap returns to the title message and the 10 s timer restarts. If a pad connects or a key is pressed, drop the message and play normally.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Dev mode\n\nReached from the pause menu, not in sessions. 10-foot legible and fully controller-driven. Tabs with L1/R1.\n\n**Sliders (live, each read by the code every step; registry in `src/core/tunables.js`):**\n\n| Tab | Variables, with defaults |\n|---|---|\n| Balance | dotInstability .6, dotAuthority 3, dotDamping 3.4, dotNoise .8, dotLag .08, ringScale 1, gustForce 1.6, mouseLeanRadius 70 |\n| Breath and reps | breathBonus .55, repLag .10, repFatigue .10, repTempoScale 1 |\n| Rhythm | stepWindow 1, stepOffsetMs 0, hoopLow .9, hoopHigh 2.4, hoopLiftRate .35 |\n| Games | headerInterval 1.0, slackWalkInst 2.6, trayGravity 9.8, trayMaxTilt 14, jogTargetCadence 3, pierBoost 2.14 |\n| Economy | dripRate 1, starThresholdScale 1, ageTrainingWeight .5 |\n\nEach slider shows its value and default. **One button resets the tab, one resets everything.** Export prints the changed values as JSON to the console and copies them if allowed, so a designer can paste them into `src/data/`.\n\n**Tools tab:** go to day 1-7; jump to any activity or scene; finish the current activity with 0-3★; give 50 Drips; unlock all; autopilot (bot skill picker); god mode (Dot can't leave the ring); time scale .25-3; overlay (scene, state, Dot, ring, fps, last device); hide HUD; free camera (`engine.setCamera({ preset: 'free' }, { syncUrl: false })`); dialogue tester (any line, with voice); sound test (every song, SFX, speaker); animation viewer (every clip on an avatar); reset save.\n\n---\n\n## 11. Attract mode\n\nAfter **10 seconds with no input on the title or any menu screen**, start a looping demo:\n\n- **Playlist:** Hub walk → Holding Still → Hoop → Header → Step → Slackline → Tray → Pier Jump → Jog → Long Stand excerpt, about 14 s each, with iris transitions. Cover every activity and feature family.\n- It runs the **real scenes** with expert bot drivers and cheats (ring ×2, god mode). Banner: {TITLE}, \"Press any button.\" plus Ounce's subtitles (\"This is a recording...\").\n- **Any input exits**: key, click, mouse move past a few pixels, wheel, pad button or stick, touch. You return to the title and the timer re-arms.\n- Not in a session, not during play, not on the pause menu.\n\n---\n\n## 12. Multiplayer\n\n**Reading of the brief:** the hub protocol is how the game plays online; on its own the game has no server, so it plays alone or on one screen. Both run the same round, **The Medley**, and the same lane code. Nothing else connects to a network.\n\n### The Medley\n\nThree events in fixed windows: Stillness (a pose), then Beat (Reps or Hoop or Step), then Balance-lean (Header), each 55 s with 10 s between, about 3.2 minutes. The specific picks and shortened durations live in `src/data/medley.js`, and the picks come from a seeded stream. Each event normalises to 0-1000; the total wins. Results show medals, awards (\"Stillest\", \"Most Apologetic\") and Ounce's remarks.\n\n### On its own: Family Hour\n\nJoin screen: **each device claims a mat by pressing Cross/Enter** (up to 4 pads plus keyboard-and-mouse). Bots can fill empty mats (toggle).\n\n**The engine merges all pads into one** ✔, so lanes read `navigator.getGamepads()` by index themselves (`applyDeadzone` is exported; guard for Node). In 4-mat staging, each player gets a small dial (radius 24) above their avatar's head. Podium, rematch.\n\n### In AI Hub: ghost mode\n\nPassed 16/16 with the real engine on WebGPU ✔ at players=1, 2, 4 (latency, jitter, loss) and host-leave.\n\n```html\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<script>/* session.js pasted unmodified: first script, right after charset */</script>\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"ghost\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Score the most across three events. Stay in the circle.\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Left stick, WASD or mouse: lean. R2, Space or click: breathe. L1/R1, F/J: step.\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">\n```\n\nBoot order ✔:\n\n```js\nlet info = null;\nif (window.AIHub?.active) info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\nconst engine = await Engine.start(firstScene, withUrlOptions({ /* ... */ seed: info ? info.seed : savedOrDefaultSeed }));\nif (info) AIHub.ready();                 // no key press, as soon as the card can show\n```\n\nIf `connect()` answers null, carry on as the normal game. Without WebGPU, `Engine.start` rejects and the engine prints \"Failed to start: WebGPU unavailable: ...\" on the page ✔. Catch the rejection, or it also surfaces as a page error ✔, and call `AIHub.fail(message)` in a session.\n\n**In a session:**\n- **The card (`card: true`)** is the game's own: the players' avatars lining up on mats in seat colours (`#e8443a #3b82f6 #22c55e #f5b700`), {TITLE}, ready ticks, how to win, the controls for the last device, the time left from the `card` event. Enter or Cross → `AIHub.answer('ready')`; Triangle or M → `AIHub.answer('more')`. Use a **direct `keydown` listener for Enter** ✔ here. No menus. Cosmetic randomness only from `AIHub.rng('card')`.\n- **Start:** on `start` show a countdown from `AIHub.time()`; play at `time() >= 0`. Event windows are read from `AIHub.time()`, so all copies stay in step.\n- **Same world:** gusts, pose picks and object waves come from `AIHub.rng(label)` or the seeded `ctx.random`.\n- **Ghosts:** a `setInterval` at 100 ms (not tied to rendering) sends `AIHub.send({ a: eventIndex, x, y, c: clipIndex, t: clipTime, s: score }, { reliable: false })` and calls `AIHub.progress({ score, label })`. Start as soon as `start` arrives, even with score 0: the harness needs both within seconds. Receivers lerp the other mats; they never simulate them, and they hide a ghost whose `a` differs from theirs.\n- **`leave`:** that avatar waves and walks off. The round goes on, host included.\n- **End:** `AIHub.result({ score, stats, awards })` once, at the end of the Medley or at once on `time-up`. On `end`: stop input, stop sound, send nothing.\n- **Never:** no title, attract, dev mode, saves, quit or restart; no chat or custom names; no `alert`, `window.open` or navigation. Names come from `info.players` and are drawn with `say()`.\n\n---\n\n## 13. Art direction\n\n**Base: the engine's native look**, default pixel pipeline, toon materials, 16-colour palette (`look` left unset). The scene reads clean and bright: white, mist, sky and cyan, with lime and sand for growth and warmth, orange and red as accents. Start with `quality: 'high'` (`'medium'` in sessions, where several copies may share a machine in testing).\n\n**Performance is out of scope.** Add the detail the scene wants and don't spend time on optimisation.\n\n### Avatars ✔\n\nRe-dress the kit's hero with the same rig. This is proven to look good at gameplay framing: egg heads, dot eyes, hair caps. Use `castShadow: false` plus `ContactShadow` ✔: casting on the model gave ugly self-shadow blotches. The hero's `Eyes` mesh reads as sunglasses, so hide it. Compile clips once and share them between avatars.\n\n```js\nfunction soften(mesh, kind = 'prism') { // same bounding box, softer shape\n  mesh.geometry.computeBoundingBox();\n  const b = mesh.geometry.boundingBox, s = b.getSize(new Vector3()), c = b.getCenter(new Vector3());\n  const g = kind === 'egg' ? new SphereGeometry(0.5, 10, 8) : new CylinderGeometry(0.5, 0.5, 1, 8);\n  g.scale(s.x, s.y, s.z); g.translate(c.x, c.y, c.z); mesh.geometry = g;\n}\nexport function dress(root, look) { // look: { skin, top, bottom, shoe, hair, long?, bun?, headband? } as palette names\n  const hide = new Set(['Moustache', 'ButtonR', 'ButtonL', 'Hat', 'Brim', 'Eyes', 'Nose']);\n  const SLOT = { Overalls: 'bottom', ThighR: 'bottom', ThighL: 'bottom', ShinR_Mesh: look.long ? 'bottom' : 'skin', ShinL_Mesh: look.long ? 'bottom' : 'skin',\n    Shirt: 'top', SleeveR: 'top', SleeveL: 'top', ForearmR_Mesh: look.long ? 'top' : 'skin', ForearmL_Mesh: look.long ? 'top' : 'skin',\n    GloveR: 'skin', GloveL: 'skin', Face: 'skin', ShoeR: 'shoe', ShoeL: 'shoe' };\n  root.traverse((o) => {\n    if (!o.isMesh) return;\n    if (hide.has(o.name)) { o.visible = false; return; }\n    if (SLOT[o.name]) o.material = toonMaterial(PALETTE[look[SLOT[o.name]]]);\n    if (o.name === 'Face') soften(o, 'egg'); else if (/Sleeve|Forearm|Thigh|Shin|Glove/.test(o.name)) soften(o);\n  });\n  const face = root.getObjectByName('Face'); face.geometry.computeBoundingBox();\n  const fb = face.geometry.boundingBox, size = fb.getSize(new Vector3()), c = fb.getCenter(new Vector3());\n  const add = (m, x, y, z) => { m.position.set(x, y, z); face.parent.add(m); return m; };\n  for (const sx of [-1, 1]) add(new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(0.055, 0.09, 0.03), toonMaterial(PALETTE.ink)), c.x + sx * size.x * 0.2, c.y + 0.02, c.z + size.z * 0.48);\n  add(new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(0.1, 0.022, 0.03), toonMaterial(PALETTE.ink)), c.x, c.y - size.y * 0.2, c.z + size.z * 0.47);\n  const hair = add(new Mesh(new SphereGeometry(0.5, 10, 6, 0, Math.PI * 2, 0, Math.PI * 0.55), toonMaterial(PALETTE[look.hair])), c.x, c.y + size.y * 0.04, c.z - size.z * 0.05);\n  hair.scale.set(size.x * 1.08, size.y * 1.04, size.z * 1.08);\n  if (look.bun) add(new Mesh(new SphereGeometry(0.1, 8, 6), toonMaterial(PALETTE[look.hair])), c.x, c.y + size.y * 0.6, c.z - size.z * 0.2);\n  if (look.headband) { const b2 = add(new Mesh(new CylinderGeometry(0.5, 0.5, 1, 10), toonMaterial(PALETTE[look.headband])), c.x, c.y + size.y * 0.16, c.z); b2.scale.set(size.x * 1.06, 0.06, size.z * 1.06); }\n}\n```\n\nAdd more hair shapes as extra meshes on the head. Good casting: player `{ skin:'sand', top:'white', bottom:'sky', shoe:'white', hair:'ink', headband:'red' }`; Coach `{ skin:'sand', top:'cyan', bottom:'cyan', shoe:'white', hair:'mist', bun:true, long:true }`, plus a plumb bob on a string (`SpringChain`) from her wrist.\n\n### Ounce ✔ (zero problems, zero warnings on the model sheet)\n\n```js\nexport const ounce = model({\n  id: 'ounce', about: 'Ounce: a mint retro bathroom scale whose round dial is its face', tags: ['character'], size: [1.1, 1.05, 1.1],\n  palette: { body: 'cyan', base: 'teal', tread: 'sky', face: 'white', rim: 'slate', tick: 'mist', needle: 'red', eye: 'ink' },\n  parts: [\n    { name: 'base', box: [1.04, 0.08, 1.04], at: [0, 0.04, 0], c: 'base' },\n    { name: 'plate', box: [0.96, 0.2, 0.96], at: [0, 0.18, 0], c: 'body' },\n    { mirror: [{ name: 'tread', box: [0.3, 0.03, 0.42], at: [0.22, 0.295, -0.22], c: 'tread' }], axis: 'x' },\n    { group: [\n        { name: 'neck', box: [0.5, 0.42, 0.14], at: [0, 0.21, 0], c: 'body' },\n        { group: [\n            { name: 'rim', cyl: [0.78, 0.1, 0.78], at: [0, 0, 0], c: 'rim', seg: 14 },\n            { name: 'dial', cyl: [0.66, 0.04, 0.66], at: [0, 0.06, 0], c: 'face', seg: 14 },\n            ...[-60, -30, 0, 30, 60].map((a) => ({ box: [0.06, 0.03, 0.09], at: [Math.sin(a * Math.PI / 180) * 0.26, 0.085, -Math.cos(a * Math.PI / 180) * 0.26], rot: [0, -a, 0], c: 'tick' })),\n            { mirror: [{ name: 'eye', box: [0.08, 0.03, 0.11], at: [0.12, 0.09, -0.07], c: 'eye' }], axis: 'x' },\n            { group: [{ name: 'needleBar', box: [0.06, 0.03, 0.22], at: [0, 0, 0.1], c: 'needle' }, { name: 'hub', cyl: [0.07, 0.04, 0.07], at: [0, 0, 0], c: 'needle', seg: 8 }], name: 'needle', pivot: true, at: [0, 0.1, 0.1], rot: [0, 180, 0] },\n          ], name: 'face', pivot: true, at: [0, 0.5, 0.08], rot: [72, 0, 0] },\n      ], name: 'head', pivot: true, at: [0, 0.26, 0.2] },\n  ],\n});\n```\n\nPivots stay movable: `build.object.getObjectByName('needle')` for mood, `'face'` for nods. Scale Ounce ×1.4 on the island and frame close in Weigh-In. Squash on hops.\n\n### Models to write as data (`src/art/models.js`; check each with `node check.mjs --sheets src/art/models.js`)\n\nKettlebell Volcano ✔ (`ball [12,9,12]`, `torus` handle, glowing top), Foam Roller Hill ✔ (a big `cyl` on its side with bands), Dumbbell Bridge ✔, medicine ball ✔, Pavilion ✔ (columns, `cone` roof, recolour per station), Sweat Jar ✔ (`{ lathe: [[.85,0],[.95,.1],[.95,2.1],[.75,2.4],[.75,2.55]], at: [0,.3,0], seg: 12 }` for the glass, plus plinth, lid and label; **toon materials are opaque, so fake the fluid**: a `sky` cylinder 1 cm wider than the wall, scaled in y with Drips, with a white highlight stripe), Rep Shed, Beat Stage with speakers, pier with railings, palm (`tube` trunk, fronds; the library has none), yoga mat, step platform, hoop (`torus`), coconut, flip-flop, golden pineapple, catapult, tray and cups, vitamin, slackline anchors, hammock, lockers, Hall of Numbers board, judges' paddles, mobility scooter, ferry, water cup, sprinkler, Kevin (body, wings, feet, with a two-pose flap).\n\nFrom the library, generic props are fine: `fountain`, `bench`, `lamp-post`, `bush`, `flowers`, `oak`, `fence`, `signpost`, `table`.\n\n### Surfaces and scene effects\n\n- **Tile floor ✔:** `textureDef({ id:'clinic-tile', size:[16,16], tile:true, palette:{ grout:'mist', a:'white', b:'white' }, layers:[{ pattern:'tiles', colors:['grout','a','b'], w:16, h:16, mortar:1, seed:3 }], about:'...', tags:['floor'] })`, added to `TEXTURE_LIBRARY`. **Never stretch a map over a box ✔** (it gave one giant tile): use a `PlaneGeometry` and scale its UVs by metres ÷ (16 / `DEFAULT_TEXEL`), as the kit's market example does.\n- **World:** `WaterSurface` ✔, `GrassField` ✔, sand and lawn as flat boxes ✔, `RippleField` at splashes, `Precipitation` in the finale, `Boids` gulls, `Decals` footprints on sand.\n- **Light:** `ctx.lights` for pavilion lanterns at dusk; `applySky(skyAt(h))` for morning and evening.\n- **Game feel:** `hitstop`, `shake`, `screen.flash`, `screen.shockwave` on the splash, iris transitions (`screen.cover`/`reveal` ✔, also resolve headless), `Trail` behind the jogger, custom particles ('sweat' in cyan, 'confetti', 'splash', 'zen' motes).\n- **Cutscenes:** ferry arrival, confession and ending with `Timeline` ✔. On the `fixed` preset, apply `tl.camera()` each frame to `ctx.camera.camera` (position, `lookAt`, fov, `updateProjectionMatrix`) ✔. Use `tl.line()` for subtitles, `tl.bars()` for letterbox.\n\n---\n\n## 14. Animation\n\nUse the engine's native system: `ClipDef` data, `compileClips`, `THREE.AnimationMixer` for class avatars, `PlatformerCharacter` on the island, procedural layers (`Squash`, `SpringChain`) for character.\n\n**Conventions** (`HERO_RIG`): facing +Z. Arm X: -90 ahead, -180 overhead. Arm Z: out to the side (R negative, L positive). Forearm -X bends the elbow. Leg -X swings forward. Shin +X bends the knee. Foot +X points the toes. Pelvis `p` offsets, `r` tips the whole body. Torso +X bends forward.\n\n**Verified poses ✔** (`validateClip` clean, `analyzeClip` no problems, reviewed on contact sheets):\n\n```js\nconst hold = (name, pose) => ({ name, frames: 60, loop: true, keys: [[0, pose], [60, pose]] });\nconst feet = (pose, R, L) => placeFeet(pose, HERO_RIG, { R, L });\nhold('Tree', { Pelvis: { p: [0.03, -0.02, 0] }, ArmR: [-172, 0, -6], ForearmR: [-14, 0, 0], ArmL: [-172, 0, 6], ForearmL: [-14, 0, 0], LegR: [-62, 0, -58], ShinR: [150, 0, 0], FootR: [30, 0, 0] });\nhold('Heron', { Pelvis: { p: [0, -0.02, 0] }, Torso: [10, 0, 0], Head: [-14, 0, 0], ArmR: [-20, 0, -80], ArmL: [-20, 0, 80], ForearmR: [-30, 0, 0], ForearmL: [-30, 0, 0], LegR: [-85, 0, 0], ShinR: [95, 0, 0], FootR: [35, 0, 0] });\nhold('Warrior', feet({ Pelvis: { p: [0, -0.2, 0] }, Torso: [0, 25, 0], Head: [0, 40, 0], ArmR: [0, 0, -90], ArmL: [0, 0, 90] }, { z: 0.38 }, { z: -0.38 }));\nhold('Chair', feet({ Pelvis: { p: [0, -0.28, -0.06] }, Torso: [24, 0, 0], Head: [-18, 0, 0], ArmR: [-110, 0, -8], ArmL: [-110, 0, 8] }, { z: 0 }, { z: 0 }));\nhold('Fold', feet({ Pelvis: { p: [0, -0.03, -0.03] }, Torso: [88, 0, 0], Head: [10, 0, 0], ArmR: [-70, 0, -6], ArmL: [-70, 0, 6], ForearmR: [-8, 0, 0], ForearmL: [-8, 0, 0] }, { z: 0 }, { z: 0 }));\nhold('Plank', { Pelvis: { r: [66, 0, 0], p: [0, -0.2, 0] }, Head: [-48, 0, 0], ArmR: [-63, 0, -5], ArmL: [-63, 0, 5], HandR: [-40, 0, 0], HandL: [-40, 0, 0], FootR: [55, 0, 0], FootL: [55, 0, 0] });\n// Scrubbed reps: keys built with placeFeet AND a feet track, or the sole dips through the floor mid-clip.\nconst squatTop = { Pelvis: { p: [0, -0.02, 0] }, Torso: [2, 0, 0], ArmR: [6, 0, -9], ArmL: [6, 0, 9] }, squatLow = { Pelvis: { p: [0, -0.3, -0.05] }, Torso: [26, 0, 0], Head: [-20, 0, 0], ArmR: [-85, 0, -8], ArmL: [-85, 0, 8] };\n({ name: 'SquatRep', frames: 30, grounded: true, keys: [[0, feet(squatTop, { z: 0 }, { z: 0 })], [30, feet(squatLow, { z: 0 }, { z: 0 })]], feet: [[0, { R: { z: 0 }, L: { z: 0 } }], [30, { R: { z: 0 }, L: { z: 0 } }]] });\n// LungeRep: the same way, low pose Pelvis p [0,-0.24,0], Torso [6,0,0], goals R { z: .34 }, L { z: -.32, pitch: 25, pivot: 'ball' }. For the left side, map poses through mirror(pose, HERO_RIG) and swap R and L goals.\n```\n\n**Still to author:** Press; StepL/StepR; header nod; flail; daze; bow; slow clap; sneeze; Coach's point and demonstration transitions; tuck and cannonball; judge raising a paddle; stepping onto Ounce; ferry disembark. Reuse kit clips: `Idle`, `Walk`, `Run`, `Sit`, `LieIdle`, `Wave`, `Victory`, `Teeter`, `Hurt`, `Fall`, `GetUp`, and more (`HERO_CLIPS`).\n\n**Preview without a GPU ✔:** `tools/clip-sheet.mjs` uses `renderSheet(model, HERO_RIG, def, clip, { frames, views: ['front', 'side'], scale: 90, trails: false, skeleton: false })` → `{ width, height, data }`, written as a PNG with `node:zlib` (`deflateSync`, `crc32`). Look at every new pose once. Hide the hat and moustache first so you judge the real silhouette.\n\n---\n\n## 15. Audio\n\nEverything is written in code. No audio files.\n\n### Music\n\n- **`ctx.audio.setVolume('music', savedMusic ?? 0.10)` at boot, every boot**, from your own settings key. The engine's default is 60%, and its stored volume key (`pixel-engine:audio`) is shared by every engine game on the origin, so don't rely on it.\n- **Write instruments loud:** track `volume` 0.45-0.8. The kit's examples use about 0.12, written for a 60% bus; at 10% × master .8 that is near silence. A test checks each song: sum of track volumes × 0.1 × 0.8 ≥ 0.03.\n- Songs are `Song` data, in `src/audio/songs.js`, each original, none imitating the source:\n\n| Song | Feel |\n|---|---|\n| Title / Plaza | gentle waiting-room bossa, about 92 BPM, soft triangle plucks |\n| Holding Still | slow, sparse, breath-paced, 60 BPM |\n| Rep Shed | light funk bass, 110 BPM |\n| Beat Beach (Hoop) and Step Class | bright, four-on-the-floor; Step is 104 BPM exactly |\n| Lagoon Games | staccato ukulele feel, 120 BPM |\n| Jog | steady, cheerful, 112 BPM |\n| Evening Report | music box, 70 BPM |\n| Long Stand | near silence, then one swelling chord line at t = 75 |\n\n### SFX\n\n`ctx.audio.register` data: needle tick, ring chime in/out, wobble warning, rep tick, step perfect/good, combo, coconut bonk, flip-flop thwap, hoop whirr (`loop`), splash, gust, gull squawk, jar drip, star pop, menu move/confirm/back, \"Ow\" stinger.\n\n### Voices: Animalese/Simlish gibberish\n\nBuild in `src/audio/voice.js`:\n\n1. **`syllabify(text, speaker)` is pure and testable in Node.** Words split into syllables; a hash of each word picks consonant class and vowel, so **the same word always sounds the same**. Output: `[{ t, dur, f0, vowel, cons, charIndex }]`. Declination -15% across a sentence; `?` rises 25% at the end; `!` +15%; `...` slows. The dialogue typewriter reads `charIndex`.\n2. **`renderVoice(ctx, destination, syllables, when)`** schedules, per syllable: a saw oscillator at `f0` through two parallel bandpass filters at the vowel's formants (a 800/1200, e 500/1900, i 300/2300, o 500/900, u 350/800, × speaker shift), gain envelope 6 ms up, 30 ms down; a noise burst for plosives (8 ms) and fricatives (40 ms).\n3. **Routing:** it works on any `BaseAudioContext`, so it renders in `OfflineAudioContext` for tests. Live, use `ctx.audio.context`, connected to `ctx.audio.buses.sfx` (undocumented but present in 0.46.0, so master and mute apply) via your own Voice gain. `ctx.audio.context` is null headless and before the first input: no-op and log.\n\n| Speaker | f0 | Syllables/s | Formant shift | Extra |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Ounce | 340 | 13 | ×1.25 | a needle tick on punctuation |\n| Coach | 165 | 7.5 | ×.9 | flat pitch, long pauses |\n| Marguerite | 230 | 9 | ×1 | slight vibrato |\n| Dennis | 120 | 11 | ×.95 | pitch up on last word |\n| June | 300 | 10 | ×1.15 | no contour at all |\n| Kevin | | | | squawk SFX, never words |\n\n---\n\n## 16. Architecture\n\nDownload the kit (the URL is in your brief) and copy the contents of the zip's top-level `pixel-engine/` folder into the dev folder, so `pixel-engine.js`, `check.mjs` and the guides sit at its root. **Never edit `pixel-engine.js`**: record its sha256 in `vendor/pixel-engine.sha256` when you unzip, and a test compares it. Fetch the hub's `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` and `README.md` into `vendor/hub/` from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/`.\n\n```\npixel-engine.js  check.mjs  GUIDE.md ...        the kit, untouched\nvendor/hub/                                     hub client and harness, untouched\nsrc/main.js                                     boot: session check, Engine.start, first scene\nsrc/app.js                                      App: scene switching, save, settings, tunables, device, debug API\nsrc/core/      dot.js drivers.js actions.js device.js tunables.js save.js net.js clock.js\nsrc/ui/        font.js menu.js dialogue.js widgets.js prompts.js screens/*\nsrc/audio/     voice.js songs.js sfx.js\nsrc/art/       avatar.js models.js textures.js clips.js glyphs.js portraits.js\nsrc/data/      title.js activities.js poses.js reps.js charts.js boards.js week.js lines.js\n               questions.js unlocks.js classmates.js stations.js medley.js about.js\nsrc/scenes/    base.js boot.js title.js attract.js hub.js weighin.js report.js locker.js records.js jar.js\n               card.js medley.js join.js ending.js  activity/{base,poses,reps,hoop,step,header,slackline,tray,jog,pier,longstand}.js\ntools/         build.mjs test.mjs clip-sheet.mjs shot.mjs\ntests/         headless/*.mjs  browser/*.mjs\n```\n\n**Everything a designer would change is plain data in `src/data/`:** poses, exercises, charts, boards, schedules, lines, unlocks, stars. A new pose, chart, board or day needs no code. That is what lets the rest of the game be built out later with normal tools, together with the live sliders and their JSON export.\n\n**Engine patterns:**\n- Start ✔: `Engine.start(new Boot(), withUrlOptions({ container: document.getElementById('app'), aspect: 'fill', touch: false, settings: { button: touchOnly ? 'top-right' : false }, quality: info ? 'medium' : 'high', seed, background: PALETTE.sky, camera }))`.\n- Each scene is a `Game`, swapped with `engine.loadGame(scene, { camera })`. It frees everything per level; keep persistent state in `App`. Transition: `await screen.cover('iris')`, `await loadGame`, `await screen.reveal('iris')`.\n- `BaseScene` owns the frame order: `update` → `App.device.update` → overlays (pause, dialogue, dev) take input first → the scene's own update → `hud.clear()` → scene draw → overlays draw. Gameplay goes in `fixedUpdate`, skipped automatically while `timeScale` is 0.\n- **Rules from the guide that matter here:** gameplay in `fixedUpdate` with `consumePress`; `wasPressed` only in `update`; all randomness from `ctx.random` forks (never `Math.random`); time from `ctx.time` (never `performance.now`); no `new PointLight`. Modules guard `document`, `window`, `navigator` and `localStorage`, so **everything runs in Node** ✔.\n- **Drivers** (`src/core/drivers.js`): `read(out)` fills `{ x, y, breath, stepL, stepR, confirm }`. `LocalDriver` (engine input and mouse), `PadDriver(index)` (Family Hour), `BotDriver(skill)`, `GhostDriver` (display only). Attract, tests, classmates and online all reuse this one seam.\n- **Debug API**, kept in the shipped game (`globalThis.__GAME__ = App`): `go(id, args)`, `state()` as JSON, `setDriver(skill)`, `tunables`. Give every scene a real `status()` line (`activity hoop | play | t 31.2 | score 412`) and a `fingerprint()` (score, Dot state).\n\n---\n\n## 17. Verified recipes\n\n### Single-file build ✔ (boots on `file://` in about 1.3 s; passes `check.mjs` and the harness)\n\n```js\n// tools/build.mjs (esbuild is on this machine)\nexecFileSync('esbuild', ['src/main.js', '--bundle', '--format=esm', '--platform=browser', '--target=esnext', '--charset=utf8', '--outfile=.build/bundle.js', '--log-level=warning'], { stdio: 'inherit' });\nconst safe = (s) => s.replace(/<\\/script/gi, '<\\\\/script').replace(/<!--/g, '<\\\\!--');\nconst html = `<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\"><head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<script>${readFileSync('vendor/hub/session.js', 'utf8')}</script>\n${HUB_METAS}\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, maximum-scale=1, user-scalable=no, viewport-fit=cover\">\n<link rel=\"icon\" href=\"data:,\"><title>${TITLE}</title>\n<style>html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: #0d0b14; } #app { position: fixed; inset: 0; }</style>\n</head><body><div id=\"app\"></div>\n<script type=\"module\">${safe(readFileSync('.build/bundle.js', 'utf8'))}</script>\n</body></html>`;\nwriteFileSync(OUTPUT_HTML, html);   // OUTPUT_HTML: the deliverable name your brief gives, in root\n```\n\nThe session client goes in **unmodified**: the hub replaces an unmodified copy with each new version. Nothing is fetched at runtime, so the game needs no CDN. Bundling doesn't count as editing the engine; `pixel-engine.js` itself stays byte-identical. Output is about 5.4 MB.\n\n### Browser flags ✔\n\n**Use all five.** With only the three in the machine notes, `renderer.capture()` failed: `mapAsync ... A valid external Instance reference no longer exists`.\n\n```\n--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader\n```\n\n### Node Playwright and the kit's check ✔\n\n`npm install playwright@1.63.0` in the dev folder. Then `node check.mjs <page> --keys KeyD*30` works on the built html if it's copied into the dev folder.\n\n### Screenshots ✔\n\nThe live loop rejects `capture()`, and a WebGPU canvas may screenshot blank. So step first, and composite the HUD:\n\n```js\nconst e = window.__PIXEL_ENGINE__; e.step(30);          // switches to manual time\nconst f = await e.renderer.capture();                   // { width, height, pixels }\nconst c = document.createElement('canvas'); c.width = f.width; c.height = f.height;\nconst g = c.getContext('2d'); g.putImageData(new ImageData(new Uint8ClampedArray(f.pixels), f.width, f.height), 0, 0);\ng.imageSmoothingEnabled = false; if (e.hud.canvas?.width) g.drawImage(e.hud.canvas, 0, 0, f.width, f.height);\nreturn c.toDataURL('image/png');\n```\n\nPut this in `tools/shot.mjs <scene> [--size 1920x1080]`. Use it only for what a script can't judge: composition and legibility. Judge the 10-foot view at 1920×1080.\n\n### Gamepad stub ✔\n\nAdd as an init script; change the state from the test:\n\n```js\nwindow.__pad = { buttons: Array.from({ length: 17 }, () => ({ pressed: false, value: 0, touched: false })), axes: [0, 0, 0, 0] };\nnavigator.getGamepads = () => [{ id: 'Stub', index: 0, connected: true, mapping: 'standard', timestamp: performance.now(), axes: __pad.axes, buttons: __pad.buttons }, null, null, null];\n```\n\nRead inputs through a frame: `moveAxis()` gave (0.8, 0.6) for axes (0.8, -0.6) in-game. Headless, `e.input.setKey('PadCross', true)` works without any stub ✔.\n\n### Hub harness ✔\n\nCopy the built html (as `game.html`) with `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` into a temp folder inside the dev folder. Serve it with `python3 -u -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` ✔, reading the port from its first output line and stopping it by its PID. An in-process `node:http` server on `127.0.0.1` and port 0 also works, but it must send `Content-Type: text/javascript` for `.js`, or the harness's module imports fail. Then for each of:\n\n```\nharness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=1\nharness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=2\nharness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5\nharness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&scenario=host-leave\n```\n\nwait for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`, then require `window.__hubCheck.pass`; print failed checks' `name` and `detail`. Each took 10-13 s with a light scene. Keep the card scene light so `ready()` lands inside the 20 s limit even with 4 software-rendered copies. Confirm the served page is yours (its title) before trusting a result. Then open the game outside a session and check it still runs.\n\n### Headless facts ✔\n\n- 600 frames with mixers takes about 80 ms, and boot about 240 ms, so full playthroughs are cheap.\n- `Engine.headless(game, { camera })`: built-ins load with no asset reader.\n- `recording()` and `replay()` reproduce the fingerprint across `loadGame`.\n- `input.setPointer(x, y, true)` drives the mouse.\n- `ctx.audio` counts plays with no context.\n\n---\n\n## 18. Testing\n\n**One command: `node tools/test.mjs`** prints only failures and one count line (`212/212 passed`). `--fast` runs the Node tests only. Rerun only after changing what a test covers. Prefer scripts to screenshots. Don't use subagents or workflows to review, judge or audit. Keep at most two browsers open.\n\n**Headless (Node), seconds:**\n\n1. **Dot:** idle bot < 20% at ring .30; average 35-65%; good > 80%; expert > 95%.\n2. **Clips:** `validateClip` empty and `analyzeClip(...).problems` empty for every clip you wrote.\n3. **Data:** every model (`checkModel`) and texture (`validateTexture`) clean; all ids resolve; `parseSong` on every song; each song passes the level check in §15; every line fits its box; every character of every string has a glyph.\n4. **Every activity:** idle bot finishes with 0★ and no error; expert bot ≥ 2★ (≥ 3★ on easy ones); sloppy < expert; result written; Drips correct.\n5. **Full scripted playthrough:** drive the real menus with `setKey` from a fresh save, bots inside activities: new week → all 7 days → every station → goals → unlock schedule → Jar milestones → Long Stand → confession subtracts exactly 7 → credits → Week 2. Assert the state at each step.\n6. **Save:** reload mid-week restores; corrupt JSON falls back safely; no storage works.\n7. **Pause:** `timeScale` 0, `fixedUpdate` frozen, menu navigable, resume exact.\n8. **Dev:** every slider changes live behaviour; reset restores defaults; every tool works.\n9. **Attract:** 10 s idle on title and on a menu starts it; no trigger during play; a full loop runs error-free over all items; any input exits.\n10. **Determinism:** record an activity, replay it, fingerprints equal.\n11. **Medley:** 4 bot lanes, scores in range, windows respected; a ghost lane never simulates.\n12. **Voice:** `syllabify` is stable, the same word gives the same syllables, a question rises.\n13. **Engine untouched:** `pixel-engine.js` hash equals the kit's.\n\n**Browser, on the built html via `file://`:**","numLines":500,"startLine":400,"totalLines":993}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01G8ZKhCwdYxtju7wyrBartQ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
