{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P5TWAyNzgFHXZNCoqC1kwE","type":"tool_result","content":"899\t**Browser, on the built html via `file://`:**\n900\t\n901\t14. Boots on WebGPU with no errors; title visible; **music volume is exactly 0.10** on first run.\n902\t15. Pad stub: ✕ confirms; prompts show PlayStation glyphs; the Settings option gives Xbox; a key press switches to keycaps; mouse move switches to mouse prompts; hover moves focus; click activates. Record each prompt state in `App.state()` so no picture is needed.\n903\t16. Phone profile with touch: message showing, ⚙ present, `engine.touch` null, attract runs.\n904\t17. Family Hour with 2 stub pads plus keyboard: three lanes move independently.\n905\t18. Audio after a real click: an `AnalyserNode` on the destination reads non-silent for SFX and music; voice in `OfflineAudioContext` has RMS > .02, and Ounce's mean pitch exceeds Coach's.\n906\t19. No layout overflow at 1920×1080, 1280×720 and 640×360: widgets record their rects, and the test asserts all fit.\n907\t20. WebKit (iPhone profile) and Firefox have no `navigator.gpu` on this machine ✔, so they can only test failure: the engine's \"Failed to start: WebGPU unavailable\" message shows ✔ and no page error is thrown. Test the touch-only screen itself in Chromium's phone profile, as in test 16.\n908\t\n909\t**Hub:**\n910\t\n911\t21. The four harness runs from section 17, all `pass`. Each harness frame is a separate copy of the game, which covers the brief's \"no second player\" note.\n912\t22. Outside a session: normal boot with `AIHub.active` false.\n913\t\n914\t---\n915\t\n916\t## 19. Build order\n917\t\n918\tFinish each step with its tests green. Keep the game runnable and the deliverable building from step 1 on.\n919\t\n920\t1. **Skeleton.** Kit and hub files, build script, test runner, boot scene on `file://`, harness passing with a stub round. Takes minutes, because the recipes above are proven.\n921\t2. **The Dot and the kit.** Dot, drivers, actions, device, tunables; font, menu, dialogue, prompts, glyphs; App, scene switching, save; Settings; pause; dev sliders.\n922\t3. **One activity, fully.** Holding Still end to end with avatars, Coach, results, voice and music. **Stop and judge the feel here**, since this is the whole game in miniature: check the bot table, then capture a run as frames and confirm the body language reads the Dot.\n923\t4. **The island and the week.** Hub, Weigh-In, stations, Report, Jar, schedule, saves. Scripted playthrough started.\n924\t5. **Other activities**, in this order: Hoop, Reps, Header, Step, Slackline, Tray, Pier Jump, Jog.\n925\t6. **The Medley.** Lanes, Family Hour, session card, ghosts. Harness at full spec.\n926\t7. **Attract, Dev tools tab, touch-only, Locker Room, Hall of Numbers.**\n927\t8. **The story and the finish.** Ferry, daily beats, Long Stand, confession, ending; line bank to 120+; all songs; every model and particle.\n928\t9. **Wrap-up.** About & Credits, exit interview, final tests, one look at each screen at 1920×1080.\n929\t\n930\t**If you must cut scope,** remove whole activities from the data, in this order: Pier Jump, Vitamin Tray, Island Jog, Overhead Mortgage. Nothing half-built ships, and nothing may look stubbed. **Never cut:** the Dot, Holding Still, Reps, Hoop, Header, Step, Weigh-In, the island, the week, the Long Stand, the Medley, attract, dev mode, Settings, About.\n931\t\n932\t---\n933\t\n934\t## 20. Finishing\n935\t\n936\t**No TODOs, placeholders, stubs or dead menu items.** Every screen works with pad, keyboard and mouse.\n937\t\n938\t### About & Credits (paged, not dense; L1/R1 or arrows or click)\n939\t\n940\tCredits; \"This is not medical advice. Ounce is a scale.\"; **Source Information** (every field your brief lists; `unknown` for anything you can't confirm; Usage: `added on import`); **Testing Feedback**; **Engine Feedback**; **Prompt Feedback**; the kit's `CREDITS.md`, shipped as the kit asks: a summary page, then the full text in a scrollable view.\n941\t\n942\t**Keep one source of truth:** `src/data/about.js` feeds the screen, and `tools/build.mjs` writes the exit-interview file from it, then re-parses it to confirm it is valid JSON. Answer the feedback questions honestly, from your real run, not from this plan.\n943\t\n944\tFor Source Information: Source is Wii Fit; Genre and Perspective as in section 1; Tech: Pixel Engine with its version, three.js r186 and Rapier as bundled in it, esbuild for packaging; Art: the engine's native pixel look; Animation: engine `ClipDef`s with `AnimationMixer`; Audio: engine `Song` and `SoundDef` data plus a Web Audio formant voice; Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, own card, 1-4 players; Family Hour is local. For Research, describe what you did yourself, and note that the director's plan included engine and hub research and spikes.\n945\t\n946\t### Exit-interview `aiHub` block\n947\t\n948\tUse the exact shape in your brief. Suggested values:\n949\t\n950\t- `name`: {TITLE}; `tagline`: yours.\n951\t- `type`: `Game`; `genre`: `Sports`; `source`: `Wii Fit`; `series`: `Wii Fit`; `players`: `1–4`.\n952\t- `controls`: `Left stick, WASD or mouse: lean. R2, Space or click: breathe. L1/R1, F/J or mouse buttons: step.`\n953\t- `tags`: `[\"pixel art\", \"comedy\", \"versus\", \"arcade\", \"3d\", \"story\"]`.\n954\t\n955\t### Your final chat reply\n956\t\n957\tIt must contain Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback, as your brief says.\n958\t\n959\t---\n960\t\n961\t## 21. Brief coverage checklist\n962\t\n963\tTick each before you stop.\n964\t\n965\t| Brief item | Where |\n966\t|---|---|\n967\t| Genre and perspective chosen | §1, §5, §7 |\n968\t| Title: riff on the source's name, picked as the brief says, by you | top of plan, §16 |\n969\t| Research: your choice; the director's is here | §4, §17, §20 |\n970\t| Single html named as the brief says, in root | §17 |\n971\t| Built on the kit; engine unchanged; own systems on top | §16, §17, §18 test 13 |\n972\t| Art: engine's look as the base, new assets for the source's feel, library for generic props | §13 |\n973\t| Animation: engine's system as the base, new animations | §14 |\n974\t| Audio: all in code, gibberish voices, music 10% by default | §15, §18 test 14 |\n975\t| Online and multiplayer: hub, and on its own | §12 |\n976\t| Dev subfolder, ports, processes, sharing the machine, `file://` first | top of plan, §17, §18 |\n977\t| Performance unlimited, no optimisation | §13 |\n978\t| Effort is yours to spend; an order and a cut list if you need them | §19 |\n979\t| Machine notes: stand-ins for controller, touch, sound, second player, iPhone, TV | §17, §18 |\n980\t| Headless tests, scripted playthrough, one command, failures and count only, screenshots only where needed, no review subagents | §18 |\n981\t| Original game inspired by the source; world, characters, themes, tone | §1, §2, §8 |\n982\t| Feature-complete vertical slice; infrastructure for building out | §3, §5, §16 |\n983\t| Dev mode from pause; standard tools; live sliders with reset | §10 |\n984\t| Attract: 10 s on title/menus, looping, any input exits, cheats allowed | §11 |\n985\t| Writing style like the source's | §8 |\n986\t| Controller first at 10 feet; native keyboard and mouse on the same screens | §9 |\n987\t| Prompts follow last input; PlayStation glyphs; Xbox option; keys and mouse | §9, §18 test 15 |\n988\t| No dense web-style screens | §9 |\n989\t| Touch-only: no touch controls, message, settings button, attract runs | §9, §18 test 16 |\n990\t| No TODOs, placeholders or stubs | §19, §20 |\n991\t| Source Information and all feedback in the chat reply and About/Credits | §20 |\n992\t| Exit interview in the exact shape, parses as JSON | §20 |\n993\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d022da92-c114-4f47-a8f5-ca68c59e3f52","uuid":"500a9df4-09fe-4b23-a21c-2d9b4cf963c7","timestamp":"2026-11-05T08:21:51.774Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-012138__x6981e3/work/PLAN.md","content":"**Browser, on the built html via `file://`:**\n\n14. Boots on WebGPU with no errors; title visible; **music volume is exactly 0.10** on first run.\n15. Pad stub: ✕ confirms; prompts show PlayStation glyphs; the Settings option gives Xbox; a key press switches to keycaps; mouse move switches to mouse prompts; hover moves focus; click activates. Record each prompt state in `App.state()` so no picture is needed.\n16. Phone profile with touch: message showing, ⚙ present, `engine.touch` null, attract runs.\n17. Family Hour with 2 stub pads plus keyboard: three lanes move independently.\n18. Audio after a real click: an `AnalyserNode` on the destination reads non-silent for SFX and music; voice in `OfflineAudioContext` has RMS > .02, and Ounce's mean pitch exceeds Coach's.\n19. No layout overflow at 1920×1080, 1280×720 and 640×360: widgets record their rects, and the test asserts all fit.\n20. WebKit (iPhone profile) and Firefox have no `navigator.gpu` on this machine ✔, so they can only test failure: the engine's \"Failed to start: WebGPU unavailable\" message shows ✔ and no page error is thrown. Test the touch-only screen itself in Chromium's phone profile, as in test 16.\n\n**Hub:**\n\n21. The four harness runs from section 17, all `pass`. Each harness frame is a separate copy of the game, which covers the brief's \"no second player\" note.\n22. Outside a session: normal boot with `AIHub.active` false.\n\n---\n\n## 19. Build order\n\nFinish each step with its tests green. Keep the game runnable and the deliverable building from step 1 on.\n\n1. **Skeleton.** Kit and hub files, build script, test runner, boot scene on `file://`, harness passing with a stub round. Takes minutes, because the recipes above are proven.\n2. **The Dot and the kit.** Dot, drivers, actions, device, tunables; font, menu, dialogue, prompts, glyphs; App, scene switching, save; Settings; pause; dev sliders.\n3. **One activity, fully.** Holding Still end to end with avatars, Coach, results, voice and music. **Stop and judge the feel here**, since this is the whole game in miniature: check the bot table, then capture a run as frames and confirm the body language reads the Dot.\n4. **The island and the week.** Hub, Weigh-In, stations, Report, Jar, schedule, saves. Scripted playthrough started.\n5. **Other activities**, in this order: Hoop, Reps, Header, Step, Slackline, Tray, Pier Jump, Jog.\n6. **The Medley.** Lanes, Family Hour, session card, ghosts. Harness at full spec.\n7. **Attract, Dev tools tab, touch-only, Locker Room, Hall of Numbers.**\n8. **The story and the finish.** Ferry, daily beats, Long Stand, confession, ending; line bank to 120+; all songs; every model and particle.\n9. **Wrap-up.** About & Credits, exit interview, final tests, one look at each screen at 1920×1080.\n\n**If you must cut scope,** remove whole activities from the data, in this order: Pier Jump, Vitamin Tray, Island Jog, Overhead Mortgage. Nothing half-built ships, and nothing may look stubbed. **Never cut:** the Dot, Holding Still, Reps, Hoop, Header, Step, Weigh-In, the island, the week, the Long Stand, the Medley, attract, dev mode, Settings, About.\n\n---\n\n## 20. Finishing\n\n**No TODOs, placeholders, stubs or dead menu items.** Every screen works with pad, keyboard and mouse.\n\n### About & Credits (paged, not dense; L1/R1 or arrows or click)\n\nCredits; \"This is not medical advice. Ounce is a scale.\"; **Source Information** (every field your brief lists; `unknown` for anything you can't confirm; Usage: `added on import`); **Testing Feedback**; **Engine Feedback**; **Prompt Feedback**; the kit's `CREDITS.md`, shipped as the kit asks: a summary page, then the full text in a scrollable view.\n\n**Keep one source of truth:** `src/data/about.js` feeds the screen, and `tools/build.mjs` writes the exit-interview file from it, then re-parses it to confirm it is valid JSON. Answer the feedback questions honestly, from your real run, not from this plan.\n\nFor Source Information: Source is Wii Fit; Genre and Perspective as in section 1; Tech: Pixel Engine with its version, three.js r186 and Rapier as bundled in it, esbuild for packaging; Art: the engine's native pixel look; Animation: engine `ClipDef`s with `AnimationMixer`; Audio: engine `Song` and `SoundDef` data plus a Web Audio formant voice; Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, own card, 1-4 players; Family Hour is local. For Research, describe what you did yourself, and note that the director's plan included engine and hub research and spikes.\n\n### Exit-interview `aiHub` block\n\nUse the exact shape in your brief. Suggested values:\n\n- `name`: {TITLE}; `tagline`: yours.\n- `type`: `Game`; `genre`: `Sports`; `source`: `Wii Fit`; `series`: `Wii Fit`; `players`: `1–4`.\n- `controls`: `Left stick, WASD or mouse: lean. R2, Space or click: breathe. L1/R1, F/J or mouse buttons: step.`\n- `tags`: `[\"pixel art\", \"comedy\", \"versus\", \"arcade\", \"3d\", \"story\"]`.\n\n### Your final chat reply\n\nIt must contain Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback, as your brief says.\n\n---\n\n## 21. Brief coverage checklist\n\nTick each before you stop.\n\n| Brief item | Where |\n|---|---|\n| Genre and perspective chosen | §1, §5, §7 |\n| Title: riff on the source's name, picked as the brief says, by you | top of plan, §16 |\n| Research: your choice; the director's is here | §4, §17, §20 |\n| Single html named as the brief says, in root | §17 |\n| Built on the kit; engine unchanged; own systems on top | §16, §17, §18 test 13 |\n| Art: engine's look as the base, new assets for the source's feel, library for generic props | §13 |\n| Animation: engine's system as the base, new animations | §14 |\n| Audio: all in code, gibberish voices, music 10% by default | §15, §18 test 14 |\n| Online and multiplayer: hub, and on its own | §12 |\n| Dev subfolder, ports, processes, sharing the machine, `file://` first | top of plan, §17, §18 |\n| Performance unlimited, no optimisation | §13 |\n| Effort is yours to spend; an order and a cut list if you need them | §19 |\n| Machine notes: stand-ins for controller, touch, sound, second player, iPhone, TV | §17, §18 |\n| Headless tests, scripted playthrough, one command, failures and count only, screenshots only where needed, no review subagents | §18 |\n| Original game inspired by the source; world, characters, themes, tone | §1, §2, §8 |\n| Feature-complete vertical slice; infrastructure for building out | §3, §5, §16 |\n| Dev mode from pause; standard tools; live sliders with reset | §10 |\n| Attract: 10 s on title/menus, looping, any input exits, cheats allowed | §11 |\n| Writing style like the source's | §8 |\n| Controller first at 10 feet; native keyboard and mouse on the same screens | §9 |\n| Prompts follow last input; PlayStation glyphs; Xbox option; keys and mouse | §9, §18 test 15 |\n| No dense web-style screens | §9 |\n| Touch-only: no touch controls, message, settings button, attract runs | §9, §18 test 16 |\n| No TODOs, placeholders or stubs | §19, §20 |\n| Source Information and all feedback in the chat reply and About/Credits | §20 |\n| Exit interview in the exact shape, parses as JSON | §20 |\n","numLines":95,"startLine":899,"totalLines":993}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01P5TWAyNzgFHXZNCoqC1kwE","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
