{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NNiwcrM43KrLLTwt5MSR7X","type":"tool_result","content":"buses={}\nbuses[t]=n}this.applyVolumes()\nbuses.sfx\nbuses.sfx\nbuses.music\n### class Settings\n\n`engine.settings`: the player's settings, applied to the engine and saved. A field the page URL\nsets (`?look=`, `?mode=`, `?res=`, `?quality=`, `?fps=`, `?debug=`: review flags) wins over a\nsaved one at start (which stays saved). `open`, `close` and `toggle` show and hide the\nsettings panel.\n\n- `new Settings(host: SettingsHost, key: string | null)`\n- `readonly key: string | null`\n- `get values: Readonly<PlayerSettings>`: The player's choices in effect: fields left out are the game's (or a review flag's).\n- `get isOpen: boolean`\n- `set(patch: PlayerSettings): void`: Change some settings: applied at once and saved. A field set to `undefined` goes back to the game's.\n- `reset(): void`: Forget every choice, the held ones too: the game's own picture again.\n- `replace(values: PlayerSettings): void`: Make `values` the settings, changing only the fields that differ: the ones it leaves out go back to the game's.\n- `onChange(fn: (values: Readonly<PlayerSettings>) => void): () => void`: Called with the values after every change; returns the unsubscribe.\n- `open(): void`\n- `close(): void`\n- `toggle(): void`\n\n### interface SettingsHost\n\n460:### class Settings\n461-\n462-`engine.settings`: the player's settings, applied to the engine and saved. A field the page URL\n463-sets (`?look=`, `?mode=`, `?res=`, `?quality=`, `?fps=`, `?debug=`: review flags) wins over a\n464-saved one at start (which stays saved). `open`, `close` and `toggle` show and hide the\n465-settings panel.\n466-\n467-- `new Settings(host: SettingsHost, key: string | null)`\n468-- `readonly key: string | null`\n469-- `get values: Readonly<PlayerSettings>`: The player's choices in effect: fields left out are the game's (or a review flag's).\n470-- `get isOpen: boolean`\n471-- `set(patch: PlayerSettings): void`: Change some settings: applied at once and saved. A field set to `undefined` goes back to the game's.\n472-- `reset(): void`: Forget every choice, the held ones too: the game's own picture again.\n473-- `replace(values: PlayerSettings): void`: Make `values` the settings, changing only the fields that differ: the ones it leaves out go back to the game's.\n474-- `onChange(fn: (values: Readonly<PlayerSettings>) => void): () => void`: Called with the values after every change; returns the unsubscribe.\n475-- `open(): void`\n476-- `close(): void`\n477-- `toggle(): void`\n478-\n--\n492:### class SettingsPanel\n493-\n494-The settings panel (DOM, like the debug panel: it stays legible at any art resolution) and the\n495-⚙ button that opens it: the player's picture, sound and engine options (`engine.settings`,\n496-settings.ts; the AudioManager's volumes). The engine pauses the game while it is open. Keys\n497-pressed in it never reach the game; Escape or Done closes it.\n498-\n499-- `new SettingsPanel(engine: Engine, container: HTMLElement, corner: TouchCorner | false)`\n500-- `readonly root: HTMLDivElement`\n501-- `readonly button: HTMLButtonElement | null`","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d022da92-c114-4f47-a8f5-ca68c59e3f52","uuid":"dec62bb0-2905-4e83-9e55-70a045afd8d5","timestamp":"2026-11-05T08:33:22.184Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"buses={}\nbuses[t]=n}this.applyVolumes()\nbuses.sfx\nbuses.sfx\nbuses.music\n### class Settings\n\n`engine.settings`: the player's settings, applied to the engine and saved. A field the page URL\nsets (`?look=`, `?mode=`, `?res=`, `?quality=`, `?fps=`, `?debug=`: review flags) wins over a\nsaved one at start (which stays saved). `open`, `close` and `toggle` show and hide the\nsettings panel.\n\n- `new Settings(host: SettingsHost, key: string | null)`\n- `readonly key: string | null`\n- `get values: Readonly<PlayerSettings>`: The player's choices in effect: fields left out are the game's (or a review flag's).\n- `get isOpen: boolean`\n- `set(patch: PlayerSettings): void`: Change some settings: applied at once and saved. A field set to `undefined` goes back to the game's.\n- `reset(): void`: Forget every choice, the held ones too: the game's own picture again.\n- `replace(values: PlayerSettings): void`: Make `values` the settings, changing only the fields that differ: the ones it leaves out go back to the game's.\n- `onChange(fn: (values: Readonly<PlayerSettings>) => void): () => void`: Called with the values after every change; returns the unsubscribe.\n- `open(): void`\n- `close(): void`\n- `toggle(): void`\n\n### interface SettingsHost\n\n460:### class Settings\n461-\n462-`engine.settings`: the player's settings, applied to the engine and saved. A field the page URL\n463-sets (`?look=`, `?mode=`, `?res=`, `?quality=`, `?fps=`, `?debug=`: review flags) wins over a\n464-saved one at start (which stays saved). `open`, `close` and `toggle` show and hide the\n465-settings panel.\n466-\n467-- `new Settings(host: SettingsHost, key: string | null)`\n468-- `readonly key: string | null`\n469-- `get values: Readonly<PlayerSettings>`: The player's choices in effect: fields left out are the game's (or a review flag's).\n470-- `get isOpen: boolean`\n471-- `set(patch: PlayerSettings): void`: Change some settings: applied at once and saved. A field set to `undefined` goes back to the game's.\n472-- `reset(): void`: Forget every choice, the held ones too: the game's own picture again.\n473-- `replace(values: PlayerSettings): void`: Make `values` the settings, changing only the fields that differ: the ones it leaves out go back to the game's.\n474-- `onChange(fn: (values: Readonly<PlayerSettings>) => void): () => void`: Called with the values after every change; returns the unsubscribe.\n475-- `open(): void`\n476-- `close(): void`\n477-- `toggle(): void`\n478-\n--\n492:### class SettingsPanel\n493-\n494-The settings panel (DOM, like the debug panel: it stays legible at any art resolution) and the\n495-⚙ button that opens it: the player's picture, sound and engine options (`engine.settings`,\n496-settings.ts; the AudioManager's volumes). The engine pauses the game while it is open. Keys\n497-pressed in it never reach the game; Escape or Done closes it.\n498-\n499-- `new SettingsPanel(engine: Engine, container: HTMLElement, corner: TouchCorner | false)`\n500-- `readonly root: HTMLDivElement`\n501-- `readonly button: HTMLButtonElement | null`","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NNiwcrM43KrLLTwt5MSR7X","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
