{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015iSAXpAU1mGweWekCVhvTV","type":"tool_result","content":"1507:- `gravity?: number`\n1785:- `static create(gravity = -24): Promise<Physics>`: Loads Rapier's wasm on first use (a separate, streamed .wasm file), then builds a world.\n1817:- `clear(): void`: Empty the world: every body, collider, joint, character and vehicle controller, trigger, tag, binding, mover, field and belt goes; gravity and the solver's iterations go back t\n2035:- `get speed: number`: Speed along the car's heading (m/s, negative reversing). Not Rapier's `currentVehicleSpeed`, which counts the up-and-down too (the suspension holding the body up against gr\n2070:- `gravity: [number, number, number]`\n2195:- `weight: number`: How hard the character presses the dynamic floor it stands on (a rope bridge sags where it stands, a spring pad sinks), in the physics world's mass units (density × m³: a 1 m \n2714:- `gravity?: number`: Downward acceleration, world units / s² (negative floats up). Default 0.\n2754:const PARTICLES: { dust: { count: [number, number]; life: [number, number]; speed: [number, number]; spread: number; flatten: number; gravity: number; drag: number; size: [number, number]; colors\n1779-Rapier world with a fixed 60 Hz step and render interpolation.\n1785-- `static create(gravity = -24): Promise<Physics>`: Loads Rapier's wasm on first use (a separate, streamed .wasm file), then builds a world.\n1786-- `world: RAPIER.World`: The Rapier world. A new one per level (`clear()`): read it from here, don't keep it across levels.\n1792-- `state(): PhysicsState`: The physics as data, between frames (`engine.snapshot()`): the fixed step's clock and the whole Rapier world, exact. Bodies and colliders keep their handles across `setState`: a game finds\n1793-- `setState(s: PhysicsState): void`: Back to `state()`: the world it saved replaces this one, bound meshes re-found by handle.\n1794-- `restoreState(s: PhysicsState): PhysicsRestore`: `setState`, undoable: the saved world is built first (nothing changes if that fails), then replaces this one; `undo()` puts everything back as it was, `commit()` fr\n1796-- `onStep(f: () => void, o: { first?: boolean } = {}): () => void`: Run `f` after every fixed step, before bound meshes (`bind`) read their bodies. Listeners run in the order they were added (instanced bodies keep t\n1798-- `conveyor(collider: RAPIER.Collider, velocity: readonly [number, number, number] | null): void`: Make a collider a conveyor belt moving at `velocity` (m/s, world axes): dynamic bodies touching it are dragged along\n1801-- `bind(body: RAPIER.RigidBody, object: Object3D): void`: Make `object` follow `body` (interpolated).\n1802-- `unbind(object: Object3D): void`","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d022da92-c114-4f47-a8f5-ca68c59e3f52","uuid":"fee4c356-9c0c-4fdc-a58d-e0d9b90b0056","timestamp":"2026-11-05T08:54:13.131Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"1507:- `gravity?: number`\n1785:- `static create(gravity = -24): Promise<Physics>`: Loads Rapier's wasm on first use (a separate, streamed .wasm file), then builds a world.\n1817:- `clear(): void`: Empty the world: every body, collider, joint, character and vehicle controller, trigger, tag, binding, mover, field and belt goes; gravity and the solver's iterations go back t\n2035:- `get speed: number`: Speed along the car's heading (m/s, negative reversing). Not Rapier's `currentVehicleSpeed`, which counts the up-and-down too (the suspension holding the body up against gr\n2070:- `gravity: [number, number, number]`\n2195:- `weight: number`: How hard the character presses the dynamic floor it stands on (a rope bridge sags where it stands, a spring pad sinks), in the physics world's mass units (density × m³: a 1 m \n2714:- `gravity?: number`: Downward acceleration, world units / s² (negative floats up). Default 0.\n2754:const PARTICLES: { dust: { count: [number, number]; life: [number, number]; speed: [number, number]; spread: number; flatten: number; gravity: number; drag: number; size: [number, number]; colors\n1779-Rapier world with a fixed 60 Hz step and render interpolation.\n1785-- `static create(gravity = -24): Promise<Physics>`: Loads Rapier's wasm on first use (a separate, streamed .wasm file), then builds a world.\n1786-- `world: RAPIER.World`: The Rapier world. A new one per level (`clear()`): read it from here, don't keep it across levels.\n1792-- `state(): PhysicsState`: The physics as data, between frames (`engine.snapshot()`): the fixed step's clock and the whole Rapier world, exact. Bodies and colliders keep their handles across `setState`: a game finds\n1793-- `setState(s: PhysicsState): void`: Back to `state()`: the world it saved replaces this one, bound meshes re-found by handle.\n1794-- `restoreState(s: PhysicsState): PhysicsRestore`: `setState`, undoable: the saved world is built first (nothing changes if that fails), then replaces this one; `undo()` puts everything back as it was, `commit()` fr\n1796-- `onStep(f: () => void, o: { first?: boolean } = {}): () => void`: Run `f` after every fixed step, before bound meshes (`bind`) read their bodies. Listeners run in the order they were added (instanced bodies keep t\n1798-- `conveyor(collider: RAPIER.Collider, velocity: readonly [number, number, number] | null): void`: Make a collider a conveyor belt moving at `velocity` (m/s, world axes): dynamic bodies touching it are dragged along\n1801-- `bind(body: RAPIER.RigidBody, object: Object3D): void`: Make `object` follow `body` (interpolated).\n1802-- `unbind(object: Object3D): void`","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_015iSAXpAU1mGweWekCVhvTV","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
