{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjYxcjiycNyLCwvjqmHb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Why Fit** is built as a single html file, and `node tools/test.mjs` passes 1137 of 1137 assertions on the final build. Not done: no ✔-marked spec item was left out. The optional dressing was skipped: sunbeams, footprint decals, splash ripples, a camera push-in, and Coach's plumb-bob string.\n\nTitled by a random pick from 50 brainstormed names. Both deliverables are in the root: `WhyFit-WiiFit-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261105-012138.html` (5.75 MB) and `exit-interview.json`, which parses as JSON. `pixel-engine.js` is untouched; a test compares its hash.\n\n## What's in it\n- **Week and island:** The 7-day week runs from ferry to Weigh-In, island, hammock and Evening Report. All 17 activities are in. The Long Stand, the confession (every shown Wobble Age drops exactly 7), credits and an open-ended Week 2 follow.\n- **Other modes:** Drop-In Class, Family Hour (local, up to four pads plus keyboard) and The Medley are in. So are a Locker Room, Sweat Jar, Hall of Numbers, dev tools with live sliders, 10-second attract mode, touch-only screen and Settings (music defaults to 10%).\n- **Online:** AI Hub ghost mode with the game's own card. All four hub harness runs pass.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-05 01:21:38\n- **Source:** Wii Fit\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** a fitness and balance minigame collection inside a light life-sim week. Isometric on the island, fixed front-on for class activities, and side-on, top-down or behind-the-back views for the other games.\n- **Tech:** Pixel Engine 0.46.0 (three.js r186, Rapier), plain JavaScript modules, esbuild, AI Hub session client 1.4.0\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's native pixel look; new models, avatars and textures written as engine data\n- **Animation:** engine `ClipDef` data through `AnimationMixer`, plus procedural lean\n- **Audio:** engine `Song` and `SoundDef` data plus a Web Audio formant gibberish voice; no audio files\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, own card, 1-4 players; Family Hour is local\n- **Testing:** headless scripts only, no subagents. Node tests cover every activity with bots, a full scripted playthrough, saves, pause, dev tools, attract, determinism, the Medley and the voice. Playwright tests cover WebGPU boot, a gamepad stub, a phone profile, two pads plus keyboard, audio, layout at 3 sizes, WebKit/Firefox failure and the hub harness. Screenshots were used for composition only.\n- **Research:** read the plan, GUIDE.md, ASSETS.md and the hub README, and searched API.md. No outside research of my own; the director's plan included engine and hub research and spikes.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** added on import\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** about 14. They included hoops being caught by accident while circling, any input failing to exit attract mode, the AI Hub card never answering Ready (no Net object), and avatars slowly tipping over.\n- **Critical:** three. The avatars drifting horizontal, any input not exiting attract mode, and the hub card never answering Ready or sending progress.\n- **Most helpful test:** the scripted playthrough through the real menus, then the hub harness.\n- **Least helpful test:** the layout-rectangle check, which stayed green while screenshots showed HUD overlaps.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** toon materials and outlines look good with no art pipeline, and `Engine.headless` makes full playthroughs cheap.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** `hitstop()` eats steps in headless runs, so tests wait for a state rather than a time. A clip with no Torso track let my lean accumulate after the mixer. The kit's clip-sheet renderer would not run in Node, so I judged poses in-engine.\n- **Most important thing I built:** the pixel HUD UI kit and the Dot with its drivers (local, pad, bot, ghost) and lane staging.\n- **Hardest part:** legibility at 10 feet with a capitals-only bitmap font and no alpha or clipping.\n- **Engine changes:** none.\n- **One change I'd make:** a retained UI layer with lowercase text, alpha and clipping.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the plan's measured Dot table, the verified recipes, the build order and the cut list.\n- **Confusing:**\n  - Space and E are both Confirm, and E is also a tab key.\n  - The hammock \"ends the day once you've done an activity\" but is also \"never a block\".\n  - Only the Dot had measured bot data.\n- **Hardest thing:** breadth with real feel in each of 17 activities without seeing them move.\n- **What I'd change:** measured bot tables per activity, tie-break rules for shared keys, and optional items marked as optional.\n\nAll of this is also on the in-game About & Credits screen."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":474,"cache_read_input_tokens":635079,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":474},"output_tokens":821,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d022da92-c114-4f47-a8f5-ca68c59e3f52","uuid":"8fc81835-3ac6-4f2b-bb67-c94631d0f0e5","timestamp":"2026-11-05T09:34:07.804Z","request_id":"req_011CgjYxcBz3TXLx8EmTzw9D"}
