PU boot, a gamepad stub, a phone profile, two pads plus keyboard, audio, layout at 3 sizes, WebKit/Firefox failure and the hub harness. Screenshots were used for composition only.\n- **Research:** read the plan, GUIDE.md, ASSETS.md and the hub README, and searched API.md. No outside research of my own; the director's plan included engine and hub research and spikes.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** added on import\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** about 14. They included hoops being caught by accident while circling, any input failing to exit attract mode, the AI Hub card never answering Ready (no Net object), and avatars slowly tipping over.\n- **Critical:** three. The avatars drifting horizontal, any input not exiting attract mode, and the hub card never answering Ready or sending progress.\n- **Most helpful test:** the scripted playthrough through the real menus, then the hub harness.\n- **Least helpful test:** the layout-rectangle check, which stayed green while screenshots showed HUD overlaps.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** toon materials and outlines look good with no art pipeline, and `Engine.headless` makes full playthroughs cheap.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** `hitstop()` eats steps in headless runs, so tests wait for a state rather than a time. A clip with no Torso track let my lean accumulate after the mixer. The kit's clip-sheet renderer would not run in Node, so I judged poses in-engine.\n- **Most important thing I built:** the pixel HUD UI kit and the Dot with its drivers (local, pad, bot, ghost) and lane staging.\n- **Hardest part:** legibility at 10 feet with a capitals-only bitmap font and no alpha or clipping.\n- **Engine changes:** none.\n- **One change I'd make:** a retained UI layer with lowercase text, alpha and clipping.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the plan's measured Dot table, the verified recipes, the build order and the cut list.\n- **Confusing:**\n  - Space and E are both Confirm, and E is also a tab key.\n  - The hammock \"ends the day once you've done an activity\" but is also \"never a block\".\n  - Only the Dot had measured bot data.\n- **Hardest thing:** breadth with real feel in each of 17 activities without seeing them move.\n- **What I'd change:** measured bot tables per activity, tie-break rules for shared keys, and optional items marked as optional.\n\nAll of this is also on the in-game About & Credits screen.","ttft_ms":2771,"type":"result","duration_ms":4347840,"uuid":"2c9515ac-8b9f-4583-9e13-ad85cc5b88ae","ttft_stream_ms":2059,"time_to_request_ms":126,"first_content_frame_ms":2059,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-sonnet-5-5":{"inputTokens":350,"outputTokens":410459,"cacheReadInputTokens":64918886,"cacheCreationInputTokens":624170,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":13.093858599999997,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":111202,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":624170,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"credential_expires_at":"2026-12-03T10:53:37.765Z"}
